1
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:20,159
You are right, Osman.

2
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,959
You are telling the truth.

3
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,799
You are Turks.

4
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,359
But there are many of us.

5
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:34,279
Just as we made the Turks kneel in this world...

6
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:37,759
...we will make you kneel the same way.

7
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:41,879
Surely, there is a Will that
makes few many and many few.

8
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:45,599
But you would never learn your lesson from that.

9
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:46,919
Don't worry.

10
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:49,959
I will cut your foolish head off.

11
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,799
Alps!

12
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,799
Today is the day to write a legend
with the blood of the infidels. Attack!

13
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,799
Attack Nokers!

14
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:15,159
Olcaytu Khan's banner.

15
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,599
Hanzade Sargun.

16
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,959
You are right, Ulugan.

17
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:21,119
It is the magnificent banner of Olcaytu
Khan, whose shadow surpasses the world and...

18
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:25,399
...whose rule brings peace
to the world that stops you.

19
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:29,919
Osman Bey!

20
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:37,839
Let not that sword be
pointed in the wrong direction.

21
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:44,239
He who always points his sword in the wrong
direction will ride his horse into wrong ways.

22
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,879
But don't worry.

23
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:50,479
We always draw our swords against you.

24
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:57,759
Now, my words are for everyone in this square.

25
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:02,479
By the command of Esenbike
daughter of Olcaytu Khan...

26
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:06,239
...this battle has ended before it began.

27
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:11,119
Today, in this square it is Esenbike alone..

28
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:16,879
...who will decide who
shall live and who shall die.

29
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:21,559
Esenbike huh?

30
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,719
Esenbike, right.

31
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:30,399
You have no way out of this forest, Osman.

32
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:37,039
You will tell me, you demon!

33
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,199
You will tell me!

34
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:42,159
Aunt...

35
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:44,439
Where is my daughter? You will...

36
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,959
..tell me!

37
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:48,639
Never!

38
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:53,879
You will never learn where she is, Bala! Never!

39
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:59,319
I will! Get up

40
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:02,799
God, what am I going to do?

41
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,759
Get up!
Get up!

42
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:07,839
I will learn Sofia.

43
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:13,479
Esenbike..

44
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:18,679
We would welcome you if you told us
you were going to come to the frontiers.

45
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,359
Osman!

46
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:24,879
Kneel.

47
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:34,519
The one whose eyes you
stare into is not your equal.

48
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,399
Wait..

49
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,279
Wait...

50
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,519
What will you do?

51
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:50,159
Will you make us kneel?

52
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:52,519
Huh?

53
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:56,679
The fate of those who tried
to make us kneel is clear.

54
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:02,719
So Ulugan...

55
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:05,239
Come on now.

56
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:09,039
If you have power show me.

57
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:11,319
Nokers!

58
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,079
Sargun!

59
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:22,839
Why did you stop your son? Let him...

60
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,079
I should let him so...

61
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:28,479
...he can do what you
couldn't do until this day, right?

62
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:32,999
My order is definite!

63
00:08:33,679 --> 00:08:35,919
This battle is over for now!

64
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:39,158
Esenbike or whatever your name is...

65
00:08:40,159 --> 00:08:41,958
You came to the frontiers.

66
00:08:42,679 --> 00:08:44,639
While you can unite with Ulugan...

67
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:47,119
...and attack us...

68
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:50,359
...you want to make an agreement with us, huh?

69
00:08:51,680 --> 00:08:56,239
Tell me. What is the
reason of your arrival here?

70
00:08:56,760 --> 00:09:02,799
It is first arresting our
short-sighted Commander Ulugan.

71
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,599
What are you going to do Altuga?

72
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:09,319
Will you draw your sword?

73
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,999
I would never my Hanzade.

74
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:19,239
What are you doing, Esenbike?

75
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,959
You did not follow Olcaytu Khan's orders.

76
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:25,199
You disgraced his name on the frontiers.

77
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:28,159
Our Khan will punish you.

78
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,439
Take him away. -Chain him!

79
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,319
Well, Ulugan, well...

80
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:52,439
I am the strongest Commander
of glorious Mongol state!

81
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:55,319
You cannot touch me! Don't you dare!

82
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,039
Ulugan!

83
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:10,719
And you, Osman Bey...

84
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,799
With my father Olcaytu Khan's order...

85
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:19,039
...I want to talk to you and
make an agreement with you.

86
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,079
If that's what you are saying...

87
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,799
..let's talk then.

88
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,479
Esebike..

89
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:33,239
Hatun.

90
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:34,999
Not now.

91
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:40,439
We will have iftar together
at Sahinkaya together.

92
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:42,559
You will listen to me there.

93
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:49,719
Nokers!

94
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:52,639
Take him!

95
00:10:55,760 --> 00:11:00,479
Esenbike, you're making a
huge mistake. I'm telling you.

96
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,919
Osman!

97
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:05,999
You're responsible for this situation!

98
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:08,079
I will make you pay for this!

99
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:10,679
I swear I will!

100
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:31,439
Boran. Cerkutay.

101
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:33,039
My Bey.
My Bey.

102
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:35,039
Follow that woman.

103
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:37,639
Watch where she goes and inform me.

104
00:11:37,920 --> 00:11:39,559
As you order my Bey.

105
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:41,959
As you order my Bey.

106
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:45,799
Now...

107
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:50,119
Now we will see...

108
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:54,679
...what that woman is
doing and what her game is.

109
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:57,639
We will reveal it.

110
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,919
And we'll know her purpose

111
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:07,759
Esenbike, huh? Esenbike.

112
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:11,519
You have to speak!

113
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,199
Sofia.

114
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:28,519
If you care about your life

115
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,999
...tell me where my sister is.

116
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:35,039
Otherwise, you're going to die here.

117
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:46,079
What do you think will happen
when I tell you where Halime is?

118
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:50,559
Who are you? Alaaddin.

119
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:55,159
What are you to Halime? Nothing!

120
00:12:57,680 --> 00:13:01,719
She's not your sister but your enemy only.

121
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:06,359
Give me patience, my Allah.

122
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:11,199
You did something evil.

123
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:13,839
But when we and my sister come together.

124
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:16,159
...everything will be as before.

125
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:18,119
Don't worry.

126
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:20,399
Just a dream.

127
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:26,639
Just a dream. That will never happen.

128
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:31,919
Bala!

129
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:36,639
Halime will never come back to you.

130
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:43,119
She's my girl.

131
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:47,079
She's my girl!

132
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,959
My daughter!

133
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:52,559
You can't call my daughter your girl, Sofia!

134
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:55,719
I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

135
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:58,799
If you call her your girl
again, I won't mind anything!

136
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:01,079
-Mom, stop. She may die!
-I'll kill you, Sofia!

137
00:14:01,160 --> 00:14:02,599
-Mother!
-I'll kill you!

138
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:05,399
-I will kill you!
-Mother, stop!

139
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:07,839
-She says she's her girl!
-Mom, stop.

140
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:10,359
If she dies, we will never know where Halime is.

141
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:12,199
Just stop.

142
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:17,399
Look what that hatun did, brothers.

143
00:14:17,560 --> 00:14:20,199
She chained Ulugan without hesitation.

144
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:24,599
Whatever goes around
comes around, brother Samil.

145
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:27,159
The one who tried to take my Bey to his Khan...

146
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:29,399
...is now going through the same thing.

147
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:31,279
Right.

148
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:39,359
If Ulugan is chained
because he couldn't beat us...

149
00:14:44,320 --> 00:14:46,679
Olcaytu's daughter.

150
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:51,839
Why would she come to our
land and make peace with us?

151
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:56,879
I can predict her purpose.

152
00:14:58,160 --> 00:15:00,119
She isn't like Ulugan.

153
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,799
A woman..

154
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:06,479
..is never like a man.

155
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:09,359
They never know what they can do, son.

156
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:11,479
So we need to be careful.

157
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:16,039
When Boran and Cerkutay
are back, we will discuss this.

158
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:21,199
Let's have a talk with Esenbike.

159
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:25,919
-We'll know what her purpose is.
-Okay, my Bey.

160
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:50,599
I'm the high commander of
the glorious Mongolian State!

161
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:54,599
Stop this disgrace! Now!

162
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:57,799
Otherwise, I will ignore the laws...

163
00:15:58,280 --> 00:16:02,199
...and break these chains here!

164
00:16:02,680 --> 00:16:06,479
Then nobody can stand against me.

165
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,119
I am...

166
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:22,399
...Great Olcaytu Khan's daughter!

167
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:26,959
The reputation of our state
got ruined because of you!

168
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,279
You will be punished, Ulugan!

169
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:38,479
If you unchain yourself now,

170
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:42,719
...Osman will put the chain
around your neck after me.

171
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:44,519
For your information.

172
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:46,999
What are you talking about?

173
00:16:47,560 --> 00:16:52,439
Osman's alps are following
us. If I release you now.

174
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:56,479
...my game will end before it even starts.

175
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:59,519
So keep crying out.

176
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:02,679
You'll know everything when we go to the tribe.

177
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:05,959
If you don't silence the prisoner.

178
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:08,919
...I will silence you nokers!

179
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,878
Come on!
We're going to the tribe!

180
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:21,279
Get off! Alright!
I can walk myself!

181
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:38,559
Look at that. You see that hatun, brother?

182
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:42,239
She's making Ulugan come after her like a dog.

183
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:44,959
I know her well, brother.

184
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:51,199
She can bury even a thousand
Ulugans, not a single one.

185
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:53,399
That's obvious.

186
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:55,519
Even you seem scared.

187
00:17:56,960 --> 00:18:02,679
Brother, her arrival won't
be good for any of us.

188
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:05,519
Let's follow them, brother.

189
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:12,079
Meryem, bring water!

190
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:16,799
-Calm down!
-Alaaddin, leave it!

191
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:19,559
She says she's her girl!

192
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:26,359
Meryem, make her drink.

193
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:29,639
If this demon dies, we'll
never know where my sister is.

194
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:33,199
-Mother. Leave me

195
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:37,799
Leave me.

196
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,039
Leave me!

197
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:42,359
Leave me! Leave me!

198
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:46,599
No mercy! Don't show mercy for her!

199
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:51,519
She doesn't deserve it! She doesn't deserve!

200
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:56,879
You're going to die soon, Sofia!

201
00:18:56,920 --> 00:19:00,679
I'll make you pay for all the sufferings
you made my daughter go through.

202
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:03,999
I will make you pay for them one by one!

203
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,919
-Mother, she may die.
-I'm going to make you pay, Sofia!

204
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:10,799
Make you pay! I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

205
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:14,519
You don't know how much she suffered, heartless!

206
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:16,199
Bala!

207
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:25,439
I never made her suffer.

208
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:29,479
If she had stayed with us,
she would have suffered.

209
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:34,999
She doesn't even remember you.

210
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:40,679
We'll see that when it's time, Sofia.

211
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:43,919
But you won't be able to see!

212
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:47,519
I'll bring my daughter back
but you won't be able to see that.

213
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:50,359
Because you're going to die!

214
00:19:51,480 --> 00:19:53,079
You're going to die.

215
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:56,479
-You're going to die.
-Alright.

216
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:03,999
I'm not going to die here, Bala.

217
00:20:06,920 --> 00:20:08,839
I'm not going to die!

218
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:20,199
I'm stronger than you think!

219
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:22,639
Stronger!

220
00:20:24,200 --> 00:20:27,719
I have many friends who
will never leave me here, Bala.

221
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:32,439
Don't trust anyone, Sofia.
Neither Ulugan nor the emperor.

222
00:20:32,720 --> 00:20:36,199
If you don't speak, nobody can take you from me.

223
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:38,679
Nobody.

224
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:42,919
Mother. Mother...

225
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:54,399
She's just under your nose.

226
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:58,239
But you'll never be able to find her.

227
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:03,479
Mother, mother.

228
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:06,759
-She won't speak, mother.
-She will.

229
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,959
One way or another, she will.

230
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:11,319
She'll either speak or die.

231
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:14,239
Mother, Sofia is smart.

232
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:17,639
She knows we won't kill her
before we learn where Halime is.

233
00:21:18,040 --> 00:21:20,519
Mother, death can't scare her.

234
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:24,279
-It'll be very hard to make her speak.
-She will speak!

235
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:28,679
First, we'll kill her hopes. She'll see
she can never get out of here alive.

236
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:31,759
Alaaddin, put her in the cage tent.

237
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:34,839
Arrange some guards. Tell
them to keep a sharp lookout.

238
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:36,519
As you order, mother.

239
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:38,199
But...

240
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:41,639
Seeing Sofia is missing they will come for her.

241
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,679
-We have to make her speak fast.
-We need to hurry up then.

242
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:47,079
No bread! No water!

243
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:50,159
When she passes out,
they'll wake her up with water.

244
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:53,759
Wash her in the cold water!
She's forbidden to sleep!

245
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:57,719
She'll speak. Drown her
in the water. Wake her up.

246
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:04,719
Meryem.

247
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:07,399
Why are you so upset?

248
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:10,559
I am...

249
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:17,959
I was thinking what she did to you.

250
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:21,719
Bala Hatun, what can I do?

251
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:25,239
-If there's anything...
You already helped, my girl.

252
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:28,239
By finding the bottle, you got Sofia caught.

253
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:29,999
Thank you

254
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:32,239
Thank you.

255
00:22:32,560 --> 00:22:35,799
Come on, come on.

256
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:17,879
Who is the one coming, Ilbay?

257
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:20,079
Enlightened in the front.

258
00:23:20,760 --> 00:23:22,399
Dark in the back.

259
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:28,119
Olcaytu's daughter.

260
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:30,399
Esenbike.

261
00:23:43,560 --> 00:23:45,799
Take Ulugan to the caged tent.

262
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:04,439
What are you looking at like that?

263
00:24:04,920 --> 00:24:06,559
Kneel

264
00:24:07,840 --> 00:24:11,119
Greet the daughter and
grandson of glorious Olcaytu Khan.

265
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:19,199
We are Turks. We do not kneel before anyone.

266
00:24:27,360 --> 00:24:28,399
Then..

267
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:37,279
..I will take your life.

268
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:52,119
All of you, either kneel or die.

269
00:24:55,520 --> 00:24:59,479
All Turks will one day...

270
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:07,439
...be buried in the carcass pit you deserve.

271
00:25:15,960 --> 00:25:19,519
I am Ilbay Bey, the Bey of the Kayi tribe.

272
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:23,799
We did not know you would come, Esenbike Hatun.

273
00:25:24,520 --> 00:25:27,439
Was I supposed to inform you, Ilbay?

274
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:35,079
I enter wherever I want, whenever I want.

275
00:25:53,560 --> 00:25:58,119
Why did you arrest Ulugan, Esenbike Hatun?

276
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:02,959
You have become the Bey's Hatun...

277
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:09,319
...but you couldn't learn that every
word should not be spoken everywhere.

278
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:20,919
Come with me to my tent.

279
00:26:26,520 --> 00:26:28,319
I guess you did not hear my mother.

280
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:32,759
Come on! Walk!

281
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:51,319
These dogs are all the same.

282
00:26:51,800 --> 00:26:55,039
They show their power with
swords against the innocent...

283
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:58,759
and then ask for peace

284
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:04,959
Sargun's eyes looked like a wild tiger.

285
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:13,799
Esenbike's desire for peace holds him back.

286
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:19,879
A tiger, huh? A tiger.

287
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:23,764
When he is allowed and
attacks, I will thrust that sword

288
00:27:23,776 --> 00:27:27,399
soaked in the blood of
the innocent, into his throat.

289
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:32,159
Then they will get out of our tribe!

290
00:27:32,800 --> 00:27:35,159
They put Ulugan in the caged tent as well.

291
00:27:36,360 --> 00:27:38,999
So, the woman kept her word, brother.

292
00:27:39,560 --> 00:27:42,119
Now she will sit on the throne.

293
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:45,559
And that is what I fear.

294
00:27:46,520 --> 00:27:50,679
Why do you fear? Will
they let her take the throne?

295
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:55,479
Brother...

296
00:27:56,840 --> 00:27:58,439
Ulugan is the shadow...

297
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:03,279
...this Hatun is the sun. She
burns anyone who gets close.

298
00:28:04,680 --> 00:28:06,759
Now everything will be much harder.

299
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:11,679
Come on.

300
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:36,479
-Bala.
My Bey.

301
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:41,159
Bala... Are you alright?
-We are alright.

302
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:44,199
We are alright. Alaeddin.

303
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:47,639
Welcome, my Bey.
-Thank you. What is the situation? Tell me.

304
00:28:48,080 --> 00:28:49,759
My daughter...

305
00:28:52,920 --> 00:28:56,239
We captured the demon Sofia,
my Bey. She is in the caged tent.

306
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:59,359
But no matter what I did, I
could not make her speak.

307
00:29:00,320 --> 00:29:04,479
We will question her. We will.

308
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:14,439
Thanks to Allah, you have brought the
Turkmen Alps safely across the border.

309
00:29:16,200 --> 00:29:20,359
Welcome, Ayaz Bey. You have strengthened
us in our difficult day. Thank you.

310
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:24,999
May the Turks live, Bala Hatun. In
this path, we are ready to die, for sure.

311
00:29:25,920 --> 00:29:33,239
-What about the other Beys? Where are they?
-They turned out to be cowards who ran away.

312
00:29:34,840 --> 00:29:37,588
I wish I could see Ulugan's
face when the Turkmen

313
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:40,359
Alps got rid of their
disguises of nokers, my Bey.

314
00:29:40,560 --> 00:29:44,117
Today, in that square, we
were about to take his life, but...

315
00:29:44,129 --> 00:29:45,319
But?

316
00:29:46,560 --> 00:29:52,679
Esenbike Hatun and her son Sargun
came with their army and stopped us.

317
00:29:55,560 --> 00:29:57,439
Who is this Esenbike Hatun?

318
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:03,119
Esenbike is the daughter of the
Mongol Khan Olcaytu Khan, Holofira.

319
00:30:04,080 --> 00:30:07,005
Now that she has arrived
in the frontiers, it will

320
00:30:07,017 --> 00:30:09,839
be more difficult to take
our tribe back, father.

321
00:31:28,360 --> 00:31:29,439
Zolzaya.

322
00:31:30,920 --> 00:31:32,999
Remove these ugly covers.

323
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:36,839
-Put the ones from Tabriz instead.
-Right away, ma'am.

324
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:06,959
From now on, on the frontiers...

325
00:32:07,960 --> 00:32:14,839
...not a single stone will
move without my permission.

326
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:21,999
Those who do not obey my order
will be treated as lower than dogs.

327
00:32:26,640 --> 00:32:28,239
Let Ulugan's fate..

328
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:31,039
...be a lesson to you.

329
00:32:33,880 --> 00:32:36,199
Now first..

330
00:32:37,160 --> 00:32:40,599
...I will finish the war that Ulugan started.

331
00:32:43,440 --> 00:32:45,959
I will make peace with Osman.

332
00:32:50,280 --> 00:32:51,399
Esenbike...

333
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:56,439
As the leader of Kayi, I
am always at your service.

334
00:32:56,760 --> 00:33:01,359
As if the opposite was possible, huh? Ilbay...

335
00:33:08,240 --> 00:33:13,439
Forgive my courage, but you
have the power to kill Osman.

336
00:33:14,160 --> 00:33:20,159
If you ask me, let's not make
peace with Osman and take his head.

337
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:48,039
I do not ask.

338
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:51,999
I do not ask anyone, I only command.

339
00:33:54,520 --> 00:33:58,799
And I take the head of those
who do not obey my order.

340
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:05,159
It is not our right to question, of course.

341
00:34:05,920 --> 00:34:10,998
We just know Osman.

342
00:34:15,360 --> 00:34:16,399
Hatun

343
00:34:16,920 --> 00:34:22,399
If you do not close your mouth soon,
this acquaintance will take you to death.

344
00:34:52,600 --> 00:34:56,359
After all that happened,
Osman will not agree to peace.

345
00:34:56,800 --> 00:34:58,519
He will have conditions.

346
00:34:58,840 --> 00:35:02,479
There is no condition that
my power cannot crush.

347
00:35:04,680 --> 00:35:07,639
Osman will have to make peace.

348
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:11,479
I will leave him no other choice.

349
00:35:52,920 --> 00:35:54,879
You have come the end of the way.

350
00:35:55,760 --> 00:35:58,279
I still have a long way to go, Osman.

351
00:36:02,400 --> 00:36:04,679
This is just the beginning for me.

352
00:36:12,720 --> 00:36:17,399
The end of your way goes through my sword.

353
00:36:18,880 --> 00:36:20,879
You will tell me where Halime is.

354
00:36:22,040 --> 00:36:24,079
And I will kill you right away.

355
00:36:24,560 --> 00:36:29,879
Osman, what do I gain in return
when I tell you where Halime is?

356
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:34,919
Will you allow me to live?

357
00:36:36,120 --> 00:36:40,399
Me, the one who made you
and your family suffer for years...

358
00:36:40,920 --> 00:36:44,559
...the one who hid your
daughter from you for ten years...

359
00:36:46,040 --> 00:36:47,959
Will you release me?

360
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:50,719
Look at me.

361
00:36:52,360 --> 00:36:53,839
You know me well.

362
00:36:54,640 --> 00:36:56,159
I don't tell lies.

363
00:36:56,960 --> 00:36:59,159
You will tell me where Halime is.

364
00:36:59,880 --> 00:37:01,479
And I will kill you.

365
00:37:01,760 --> 00:37:03,679
Then forget about your daughter.

366
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:09,479
Osman, I will never tell you where she is.

367
00:37:11,280 --> 00:37:13,239
Then you will rot here.

368
00:37:13,240 --> 00:37:17,719
While I rot here you will never...

369
00:37:18,400 --> 00:37:21,719
...reunite with your baby gazelle.

370
00:37:24,920 --> 00:37:30,719
You will tell me where
Halime is, or I'll kill you!

371
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:33,559
We will make a deal, Osman.

372
00:37:36,480 --> 00:37:37,879
We will make a deal.

373
00:37:38,880 --> 00:37:41,639
If you set me free...

374
00:37:46,120 --> 00:37:48,479
...I will give your daughter back to you.

375
00:37:50,240 --> 00:37:51,519
Or else..

376
00:37:52,960 --> 00:37:55,239
...you will never be able to find her.

377
00:37:55,560 --> 00:37:57,119
We won't make a deal.

378
00:37:59,080 --> 00:38:01,319
You will die!

379
00:38:01,320 --> 00:38:03,719
Osman. Osman, stop.

380
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:06,519
Osman, stop!

381
00:38:06,520 --> 00:38:09,999
Don't.. Please, don't! She is the
only one who knows where Halime is!

382
00:38:10,080 --> 00:38:11,559
-Bala.
-Osman.

383
00:38:11,560 --> 00:38:15,239
Let's not lose our daughter once again.
-Bala... -She will speak!

384
00:38:15,440 --> 00:38:18,039
She will speak. I promise, she will. Don't.

385
00:38:19,360 --> 00:38:21,079
Let's not lose her, please.

386
00:38:30,360 --> 00:38:31,679
It's your decision.

387
00:38:32,920 --> 00:38:35,679
You have the chance to convince Osman.

388
00:38:36,520 --> 00:38:38,719
If you set me free

389
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:43,959
...your ten years of pain
for your child will end.

390
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:11,039
Osman.

391
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:13,919
-Bala...
My Osman.

392
00:39:16,320 --> 00:39:19,246
To reunite with my Halime,
with our daughter, I am

393
00:39:19,258 --> 00:39:22,599
holding on to even the smallest
hope and chasing after it.

394
00:39:25,080 --> 00:39:26,119
Osman.

395
00:39:27,480 --> 00:39:29,839
My Bey! My Bey!

396
00:39:37,720 --> 00:39:40,279
-Peace be upon you
-Peace be upon you, my Bey.

397
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:42,279
Peace be upon you too, tell me.

398
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:45,479
Did that Hatun loosen Ulugan's chains?

399
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:48,639
Ulugan did everything he could
to save himself, my Bey, but...

400
00:39:49,040 --> 00:39:51,719
...they did not give him a chance for a moment.

401
00:39:51,720 --> 00:39:55,879
My Bey, they dragged him like a dog
with chains and threw him into the tent.

402
00:39:56,160 --> 00:40:00,839
His nokers could not even look at
him out of respect for Esenbike Hatun.

403
00:40:03,760 --> 00:40:06,839
It seems the snake is changing its skin, huh?

404
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:10,479
What will happen now, my Bey?

405
00:40:12,600 --> 00:40:15,359
We will accept that Hatun's invitation.

406
00:40:16,760 --> 00:40:19,079
Then we will understand her intentions.

407
00:40:52,800 --> 00:40:53,839
Get out

408
00:41:13,960 --> 00:41:15,839
This plan you made...

409
00:41:17,200 --> 00:41:21,639
It better be worth disgracing me, Esenbike.

410
00:41:27,600 --> 00:41:30,719
Don't talk as if you don't know me, Ulugan.

411
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:36,519
Once I get my teeth into something,
I do not let go without tearing it apart.

412
00:41:37,200 --> 00:41:38,439
Don't worry.

413
00:41:40,800 --> 00:41:46,679
When I am done with Osman, you
will be the only ruler of the frontiers.

414
00:41:58,160 --> 00:42:00,079
What is this great plan?

415
00:42:01,000 --> 00:42:04,319
What is this game, this plan for?

416
00:42:04,960 --> 00:42:07,519
I will make an agreement with Osman.

417
00:42:09,080 --> 00:42:11,999
Tonight, I will present my conditions to him.

418
00:42:13,280 --> 00:42:14,839
Agreement for what?

419
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:17,679
Osman will either pay taxes...

420
00:42:18,800 --> 00:42:23,679
...or let his daughter Fatma marry my son.

421
00:42:25,800 --> 00:42:28,039
Either way, we will win.

422
00:42:28,600 --> 00:42:30,439
Don't even try...

423
00:42:31,480 --> 00:42:34,119
Osman will never accept this.

424
00:42:34,800 --> 00:42:38,759
Then open your ears and
listen to me carefully, Ulugan.

425
00:42:39,520 --> 00:42:41,639
Osman has no other choice.

426
00:42:42,320 --> 00:42:44,039
You have struck the blow.

427
00:42:45,640 --> 00:42:49,319
But I will be the one to tear his heart out.

428
00:42:52,400 --> 00:42:56,359
He will have to kneel.

429
00:42:58,640 --> 00:43:00,159
How will you succeed?

430
00:43:01,760 --> 00:43:03,399
Not just me...

431
00:43:04,360 --> 00:43:06,319
...we will do it together.

432
00:43:09,520 --> 00:43:12,599
While I am meeting with Osman...

433
00:43:17,880 --> 00:43:19,839
...you will escape from here.

434
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:29,439
What is this game for?

435
00:43:44,440 --> 00:43:47,999
Esenbike... She has great power.

436
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:51,399
She does.

437
00:43:51,880 --> 00:43:54,679
Nobody in the frontiers can compete with her.

438
00:43:55,320 --> 00:43:57,319
But I'm not afraid of her power...

439
00:43:57,760 --> 00:44:00,239
...but that she wants to make peace with Osman.

440
00:44:00,960 --> 00:44:04,159
We should find out her purpose first.

441
00:44:05,800 --> 00:44:07,119
No.

442
00:44:08,040 --> 00:44:09,679
Whatever her purpose is.

443
00:44:09,680 --> 00:44:13,359
...she'll throw us under Osman's
feet without hesitation to make peace.

444
00:44:13,360 --> 00:44:15,999
-Didn't you see her? -Osman won't kneel.

445
00:44:16,400 --> 00:44:18,439
And he won't make peace, Ilbay.

446
00:44:19,080 --> 00:44:23,039
It's better if he does. But I
won't let that happen, Begum.

447
00:44:25,400 --> 00:44:26,879
Never.

448
00:44:39,440 --> 00:44:43,959
Come on, hurry up! Prepare
the table immediately!

449
00:44:46,840 --> 00:44:52,119
My father Olcaytu Khan wanted
Osman's head under his feet.

450
00:44:52,520 --> 00:44:55,239
But you convinced him about this game, mother.

451
00:44:55,320 --> 00:44:59,679
So... What do you think we should do now?

452
00:45:00,280 --> 00:45:04,799
If he comes here and turns down our offer.

453
00:45:06,160 --> 00:45:10,239
...we should drink Osman's
blood instead of water in this table.

454
00:45:11,840 --> 00:45:13,519
You're so immature, Sargun.

455
00:45:13,960 --> 00:45:17,639
You don't see for what purpose I'm doing this.

456
00:45:21,360 --> 00:45:23,119
Today or tomorrow.

457
00:45:23,280 --> 00:45:28,839
...Osman will have to accept our offer.

458
00:45:35,280 --> 00:45:37,159
Esenbike Hatun.

459
00:45:37,760 --> 00:45:39,559
Osman Bey is here.

460
00:45:43,320 --> 00:45:48,119
Destroying Osman who
damaged Mongolians so much...

461
00:45:48,320 --> 00:45:50,719
...would only make him a hero.

462
00:45:52,120 --> 00:45:56,759
We'll wipe him out of
the world with the politics.

463
00:46:10,920 --> 00:46:13,279
Esenbike Hatun.

464
00:46:14,120 --> 00:46:18,159
I knew you wouldn't turn
down my invitation, Osman Bey.

465
00:46:19,240 --> 00:46:21,159
Welcome.

466
00:46:23,120 --> 00:46:25,879
We aren't here to eat.

467
00:46:26,520 --> 00:46:29,079
We're here to hear you.

468
00:46:30,680 --> 00:46:33,399
We will talk. We will talk.

469
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:39,439
Time is coming.
Let's break fast first.

470
00:47:11,800 --> 00:47:13,279
My Allah.

471
00:47:13,440 --> 00:47:16,599
I'm before You with the prayer of Hadhrat Jacob.

472
00:47:16,960 --> 00:47:19,879
You helped him and Joseph come back together.

473
00:47:20,240 --> 00:47:22,719
So help me and my daughter come back together.

474
00:47:23,440 --> 00:47:26,559
You are the One Who
accepts the prayers, my Allah.

475
00:47:27,680 --> 00:47:32,359
Please fulfill our longings and
make our ways join together.

476
00:47:34,800 --> 00:47:36,119
Aameen.

477
00:47:36,520 --> 00:47:38,359
-Aameen.
-Aameen.

478
00:47:40,480 --> 00:47:42,279
May Allah accept.

479
00:47:42,800 --> 00:47:45,399
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

480
00:47:48,600 --> 00:47:50,199
Thanks, mother.

481
00:47:51,240 --> 00:47:52,839
Thank you, mother.

482
00:47:55,720 --> 00:47:57,079
Here.

483
00:48:05,520 --> 00:48:08,319
-In the name of Allah.
-Bala Hatun.

484
00:48:08,760 --> 00:48:11,839
You need to break your fast. You need energy.

485
00:48:15,680 --> 00:48:17,679
Thank you, my girl.

486
00:48:22,920 --> 00:48:25,439
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

487
00:48:29,400 --> 00:48:31,599
Are you thinking about Sofia?

488
00:48:34,880 --> 00:48:36,239
No.

489
00:48:37,040 --> 00:48:40,479
Thinking about my Halime.

490
00:48:42,120 --> 00:48:45,279
Sofia raised her like a Christian.

491
00:48:45,680 --> 00:48:47,439
But I don't get it.

492
00:48:47,600 --> 00:48:50,199
How can she not remember us?

493
00:48:51,280 --> 00:48:56,039
She forgot her mother, father,
brothers and even her real name.

494
00:48:58,520 --> 00:48:59,919
Mother.

495
00:49:00,480 --> 00:49:03,159
She was too young when she was abducted.

496
00:49:03,480 --> 00:49:05,879
Who knows what Sofia did to her?

497
00:49:06,040 --> 00:49:09,839
She's cruel enough to take
away a little child from her family.

498
00:49:11,040 --> 00:49:12,999
She can do anything.

499
00:49:14,360 --> 00:49:16,439
Maybe, she didn't forget.

500
00:49:17,080 --> 00:49:20,479
Maybe, Sofia is saying so to hurt you.

501
00:49:26,520 --> 00:49:31,039
Besides, even if a child forget everything.

502
00:49:31,480 --> 00:49:34,959
...she can never forget the
affection that her parents gave her.

503
00:49:36,440 --> 00:49:38,399
Gonca is right, mother.

504
00:49:38,920 --> 00:49:41,599
Good memories can never be forgotten.

505
00:49:41,800 --> 00:49:46,279
You'll see. When Halime is back,
everything will be better than before.

506
00:49:47,800 --> 00:49:50,199
-God willing.
-God willing.

507
00:49:51,400 --> 00:49:54,759
Especially her first fast.
She was just a little kid.

508
00:49:55,080 --> 00:49:59,159
But she insisted on fasting. Remember, Bala?

509
00:49:59,320 --> 00:50:01,159
Yes. How can I even forget?

510
00:50:01,160 --> 00:50:05,479
She almost passed out due to hunger.
And her father could hardly convince her.

511
00:50:05,480 --> 00:50:08,599
She broke her fast in the afternoon azan.

512
00:50:14,400 --> 00:50:15,879
Meryem.

513
00:50:16,080 --> 00:50:18,279
Do you remember your first fast?

514
00:50:22,680 --> 00:50:23,919
No.

515
00:50:24,320 --> 00:50:26,039
I don't remember.

516
00:50:26,840 --> 00:50:29,279
It means you were too young...

517
00:50:29,600 --> 00:50:31,439
...when you first fasted, my girl.

518
00:50:38,880 --> 00:50:41,039
What if Sofia doesn't speak?

519
00:50:42,880 --> 00:50:44,359
She will.

520
00:50:44,880 --> 00:50:48,519
Her collaborator Ulugan who
could save her is gone now.

521
00:50:49,080 --> 00:50:50,639
She'll lose her hopes.

522
00:50:50,840 --> 00:50:53,519
She has to speak.

523
00:51:12,120 --> 00:51:16,639
Well... You invited us to the iftar.

524
00:51:17,400 --> 00:51:19,399
So we shared your food.

525
00:51:21,760 --> 00:51:24,159
You say come to the point now.

526
00:51:25,840 --> 00:51:29,839
Esenbike Hatun, you took Ulugan from me.

527
00:51:31,160 --> 00:51:35,159
And you said you wanted to make peace.

528
00:51:36,560 --> 00:51:41,919
Tell me. What is your purpose
of coming to the frontiers?

529
00:51:45,040 --> 00:51:49,079
My purpose is nothing more
than you heard, Osman Bey.

530
00:51:50,160 --> 00:51:55,439
I came to end the war
that Ulugan and you started.

531
00:51:55,760 --> 00:51:57,919
Whose soldier is Ulugan?

532
00:51:59,680 --> 00:52:02,039
Why did he come to the frontiers?

533
00:52:02,720 --> 00:52:06,479
He wanted to make me kneel
as Olcaytu Khan's soldier.

534
00:52:07,960 --> 00:52:09,759
In these lands,

535
00:52:10,160 --> 00:52:12,519
...there is peace if you want peace...

536
00:52:12,680 --> 00:52:14,999
...and there is war if you want war.

537
00:52:15,440 --> 00:52:17,039
But you should know this.

538
00:52:17,360 --> 00:52:19,999
No annexation.

539
00:52:21,240 --> 00:52:23,119
You have to stop there.

540
00:52:29,360 --> 00:52:33,199
This is the part where you are wrong, Osman Bey.

541
00:52:34,440 --> 00:52:37,159
You don't look into the matter.

542
00:52:38,160 --> 00:52:41,079
You just see the names and titles.

543
00:52:42,800 --> 00:52:48,279
We promise you a range that you can't even see.

544
00:52:55,960 --> 00:52:59,319
What's the thing I can't see?

545
00:53:01,080 --> 00:53:04,159
Open my eyes then, Esenbike Hatun.

546
00:53:07,160 --> 00:53:08,959
You Turks..

547
00:53:09,600 --> 00:53:13,479
If you take the right side,

548
00:53:14,080 --> 00:53:17,879
...you won't be a threat against
but a gain in the west for...

549
00:53:19,080 --> 00:53:24,239
...the Ilkhanid State that
is flourishing in the east.

550
00:53:31,120 --> 00:53:32,839
So...

551
00:53:34,480 --> 00:53:36,799
You tell me to fight Byzantine...

552
00:53:36,920 --> 00:53:40,639
...while Mongolians are
fighting in the east, right?

553
00:53:41,600 --> 00:53:44,079
I'm talking about alliance.

554
00:53:44,120 --> 00:53:46,679
But you call it annexation.

555
00:53:46,880 --> 00:53:49,159
What does it matter, Osman Bey?

556
00:53:49,800 --> 00:53:54,319
You'll find peace under the
shadow of the victorious one.

557
00:53:55,840 --> 00:53:59,239
This alliance can make
the whole world one state.

558
00:54:00,040 --> 00:54:02,119
Just think about the consequence.

559
00:54:04,600 --> 00:54:10,039
But this gift will have a price.

560
00:54:12,080 --> 00:54:13,359
Tell me now.

561
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:17,999
How can we even find peace
under the shadow of Mongolians?

562
00:54:19,800 --> 00:54:22,359
You're a smart man, Osman Bey.

563
00:54:22,600 --> 00:54:24,999
But let me explain.

564
00:54:26,040 --> 00:54:31,599
You have to pay taxes like the
other states under our authority.

565
00:54:43,000 --> 00:54:46,199
My answer to this question...

566
00:54:48,440 --> 00:54:50,239
...is known by everyone.

567
00:54:51,080 --> 00:54:53,999
I told Ulugan. Now I'll tell you.

568
00:54:58,040 --> 00:55:03,079
Not a single coin from my
treasure or my people's pouches...

569
00:55:03,120 --> 00:55:05,359
...is going to Mongolians.

570
00:55:06,880 --> 00:55:09,199
I know. I know.

571
00:55:10,880 --> 00:55:14,279
I know you can't pay the tax...

572
00:55:15,320 --> 00:55:18,159
...even if you accept our offer.

573
00:55:20,480 --> 00:55:26,039
For this reason, I have another offer for you.

574
00:55:27,040 --> 00:55:28,959
I've heard...

575
00:55:30,640 --> 00:55:33,919
...that you have a beautiful
daughter called Fatma.

576
00:55:34,040 --> 00:55:36,359
-Father!
-What is she saying, my Bey?

577
00:55:36,440 --> 00:55:38,039
Wait.

578
00:55:53,040 --> 00:55:56,039
This won't make us enemies...

579
00:55:56,600 --> 00:55:59,159
...but relatives, Osman Bey.

580
00:56:01,040 --> 00:56:05,119
If you make your daughter
Fatma marry my son Sargun

581
00:56:06,960 --> 00:56:09,999
...you'll be subject to the
Ilkhanid State without taxes...

582
00:56:10,240 --> 00:56:13,839
...and be our most powerful
commander in the west.

583
00:56:13,880 --> 00:56:15,519
Well..

584
00:56:18,840 --> 00:56:21,119
You invited us to your table.

585
00:56:21,560 --> 00:56:23,359
Thank you.

586
00:56:23,680 --> 00:56:26,279
I always have respect for the host.

587
00:56:26,560 --> 00:56:28,639
But what you said will never happen.

588
00:56:29,760 --> 00:56:31,799
I won't let that happen.

589
00:56:32,080 --> 00:56:34,359
My word is final!

590
00:56:34,720 --> 00:56:36,999
You have to pay the tax!

591
00:56:38,160 --> 00:56:40,599
You have two days.

592
00:56:55,279 --> 00:56:57,009
Osman Bey Secret Tents

593
00:56:57,040 --> 00:57:00,199
Bala Hatun's orders. Nobody can go in.

594
00:57:00,640 --> 00:57:03,799
I've brought bread and water.
She shouldn't die of hunger.

595
00:57:05,080 --> 00:57:07,719
She should die but...

596
00:57:08,040 --> 00:57:10,239
...she has to live to speak.

597
00:57:10,280 --> 00:57:13,519
You're right. Go. But come out quickly.

598
00:57:28,400 --> 00:57:29,999
Poena.

599
00:57:30,960 --> 00:57:33,879
-What ate you doing here?
-Aunt.

600
00:57:41,680 --> 00:57:42,919
Aunt.

601
00:57:43,280 --> 00:57:45,319
I've brought bread and water for you.

602
00:57:45,960 --> 00:57:48,879
Don't worry. I'll get you out of here.
-No, no.

603
00:57:50,480 --> 00:57:52,199
I can't put you in danger.

604
00:57:52,400 --> 00:57:55,919
Just send a message to
Hristo. Tell him where I am.

605
00:57:56,320 --> 00:58:00,079
He and Ulugan will burn down this place.

606
00:58:00,880 --> 00:58:02,359
That's not possible.

607
00:58:03,040 --> 00:58:06,279
A woman called Esenbike has come.
-Esenbike?

608
00:58:06,720 --> 00:58:08,919
They said she chained Ulugan.

609
00:58:09,120 --> 00:58:10,919
Olcaytu's daughter.

610
00:58:12,800 --> 00:58:17,759
Damn it. What is she doing here?

611
00:58:19,120 --> 00:58:22,799
I'll try to send a message to Hristo.

612
00:58:23,800 --> 00:58:28,399
But if Bala finds out that
you lied about Halime,

613
00:58:28,480 --> 00:58:32,199
...they will kill you.

614
00:58:35,560 --> 00:58:37,119
My little bird.

615
00:58:37,760 --> 00:58:41,479
I opened such a wound inside them...

616
00:58:43,120 --> 00:58:45,119
Hey, look at me.

617
00:58:46,760 --> 00:58:49,479
They can't do anything to me.

618
00:58:51,440 --> 00:58:53,199
Aunt.

619
00:58:54,480 --> 00:58:57,759
Halime is really dead.

620
00:58:58,800 --> 00:58:59,999
Isn't she?

621
00:59:01,280 --> 00:59:05,359
Of course. I'm just using my enemy's weakness.

622
00:59:07,480 --> 00:59:09,039
Why did you ask?

623
00:59:09,480 --> 00:59:11,479
You're saying such words...

624
00:59:12,160 --> 00:59:13,719
...that it's like real.

625
00:59:14,040 --> 00:59:15,679
Even I believe you.

626
00:59:16,800 --> 00:59:19,599
I'm a good liar, my little bird.

627
00:59:20,640 --> 00:59:22,719
Are you taking your medicine?

628
00:59:25,000 --> 00:59:29,279
Do you care about me even in such a situation?

629
00:59:29,280 --> 00:59:32,279
Poena, you are very precious to me.

630
00:59:32,720 --> 00:59:34,079
Very precious.

631
00:59:34,760 --> 00:59:37,679
Don't forget to take your medicine.

632
00:59:38,280 --> 00:59:40,519
Don't worry. I'm taking it.

633
00:59:44,840 --> 00:59:47,879
Beat her well. She has to speak.

634
00:59:48,080 --> 00:59:51,559
As you order, Bala Hatun. One
way or another, I'll make her speak.

635
00:59:54,520 --> 00:59:56,599
I'm glad I have you, aunt.

636
00:59:58,120 --> 01:00:02,199
I will do my best to save you from here.

637
01:00:02,240 --> 01:00:04,159
Don't be sad.

638
01:00:05,840 --> 01:00:08,079
This doesn't suit you at all.

639
01:00:08,800 --> 01:00:13,119
Poena, both you and I are very strong.

640
01:00:14,720 --> 01:00:17,279
And I'll get out of here.

641
01:00:22,560 --> 01:00:24,599
You little fool!

642
01:00:24,760 --> 01:00:26,919
You little demon!

643
01:00:27,120 --> 01:00:30,399
-You think I will speak to you?
-What's going on?

644
01:00:30,680 --> 01:00:33,439
What are you doing here, Meryem?
-I am...

645
01:00:34,960 --> 01:00:36,559
I wanted to make her speak.

646
01:00:36,760 --> 01:00:39,879
I wanted to end your suffering.

647
01:00:42,440 --> 01:00:46,599
-How did you get in here?
-Sisters were bringing bread and water.

648
01:00:47,160 --> 01:00:49,079
I said I'd take them.

649
01:00:50,000 --> 01:00:51,439
Bala.

650
01:00:51,640 --> 01:00:55,639
Did you send your tail to me
thinking she can convince me?

651
01:00:57,400 --> 01:00:59,559
I won't speak, Bala.

652
01:01:00,480 --> 01:01:05,119
Convince Osman to promise
that he will release me.

653
01:01:05,280 --> 01:01:09,479
Kismet! Nobody but you will go in here!

654
01:01:11,320 --> 01:01:14,079
You get out. We will talk.

655
01:01:22,680 --> 01:01:24,239
Are you hungry, Sofia?

656
01:01:24,360 --> 01:01:26,599
I know you don't want to die.

657
01:01:27,160 --> 01:01:28,999
A last chance for you.

658
01:01:29,560 --> 01:01:34,879
If you speak now, you can sleep
comfortably one last time tonight.

659
01:01:35,840 --> 01:01:39,639
-If you don't speak, it's your choice.
-Bala.

660
01:01:40,320 --> 01:01:43,319
Will you torture me with hunger?

661
01:01:55,920 --> 01:01:58,639
I come from hell.

662
01:01:59,600 --> 01:02:03,239
And in front of you, this
is not Sofia that you know.

663
01:02:06,280 --> 01:02:07,519
You try to..

664
01:02:08,560 --> 01:02:10,799
...make me give up..

665
01:02:13,160 --> 01:02:15,839
...but we will see who gives up.

666
01:02:18,080 --> 01:02:19,679
We'll see Sofia.

667
01:02:20,240 --> 01:02:21,399
We'll see.

668
01:02:28,040 --> 01:02:30,639
-No...
We'll see!

669
01:02:31,680 --> 01:02:32,999
No!

670
01:02:33,680 --> 01:02:34,719
No!

671
01:02:35,800 --> 01:02:36,999
No!

672
01:02:37,600 --> 01:02:40,759
No!

673
01:02:51,960 --> 01:02:53,599
Remember, Osman Bey.

674
01:02:54,440 --> 01:02:57,479
You have two days. No more.

675
01:02:58,560 --> 01:03:04,439
You will either pay the tax or give
your daughter as a bride to our family.

676
01:03:05,960 --> 01:03:11,319
Think about what I said. Come
to me with a positive answer.

677
01:03:14,000 --> 01:03:15,199
Or else..

678
01:03:21,040 --> 01:03:23,879
Or what?

679
01:03:24,880 --> 01:03:26,239
Esenbike Hatun.

680
01:03:31,320 --> 01:03:35,279
Or the light of this world will go out for Kayi.

681
01:03:36,480 --> 01:03:41,559
So many lives will be lost.
These lands will be ruined.

682
01:03:46,240 --> 01:03:47,799
Even if we are ruined...

683
01:03:49,520 --> 01:03:53,079
...even if we die on this path...

684
01:03:53,920 --> 01:03:55,679
...we will never give up.

685
01:03:57,800 --> 01:03:58,839
Don't...

686
01:03:59,920 --> 01:04:01,839
...worry about it.

687
01:04:05,560 --> 01:04:06,759
Esenbike Hatun.

688
01:04:09,480 --> 01:04:12,287
Rebel Ulugan escaped from
Kayi tribe, Esenbike Hatun.

689
01:04:12,299 --> 01:04:13,239
What?

690
01:04:13,520 --> 01:04:15,199
Ulugan escaped, huh?

691
01:04:16,240 --> 01:04:19,719
You couldn't even keep
a dog in a cage. Get lost!

692
01:04:20,440 --> 01:04:21,479
Sargun.

693
01:04:22,360 --> 01:04:26,399
Go after them immediately.
Bring and throw him at my feet.

694
01:04:30,880 --> 01:04:37,759
Even though Olcaytu Khan wanted you alive,
what you did brought your death, Ulugan.

695
01:04:40,360 --> 01:04:43,399
You should also be careful, Osman Bey.

696
01:04:47,800 --> 01:04:51,279
Ulugan will first attack you.

697
01:04:53,880 --> 01:04:57,359
He will want to prevent the peace we made.

698
01:04:57,880 --> 01:04:59,079
We'll see.

699
01:05:02,640 --> 01:05:04,239
We'll see.

700
01:05:15,120 --> 01:05:18,439
Esenbike's arrival is not good, Ulugan.

701
01:05:19,280 --> 01:05:22,399
But she has planned her game well.

702
01:05:30,400 --> 01:05:31,439
A wolf...

703
01:05:32,560 --> 01:05:34,439
...cannot be deceived by games.

704
01:05:35,920 --> 01:05:40,079
Osman will neither give
his daughter nor pay the tax.

705
01:05:44,680 --> 01:05:46,039
Esenbike..

706
01:05:47,800 --> 01:05:50,119
...left the palace.

707
01:05:50,720 --> 01:05:52,879
But this is the Anatolian plain.

708
01:05:54,320 --> 01:05:59,679
Here, we walk over the heads
that are cut off from their bodies.

709
01:06:03,920 --> 01:06:05,999
Esenbike will learn this as well.

710
01:06:08,880 --> 01:06:12,959
Does Osman have a choice to make a move, Ulugan?

711
01:06:13,680 --> 01:06:17,199
Esenbike can destroy him with just one order.

712
01:06:19,320 --> 01:06:20,959
Not just Esenbike...

713
01:06:22,360 --> 01:06:28,639
...even if Olcaytu Khan comes from Tabriz
no one can take Osman from my hands.

714
01:06:30,600 --> 01:06:32,599
I will take his life.

715
01:06:35,240 --> 01:06:37,119
Ulugan.

716
01:06:38,200 --> 01:06:39,559
Your path is my path.

717
01:06:40,560 --> 01:06:43,799
I will do as you say even if I
have to put my life at risk. But...

718
01:06:45,120 --> 01:06:47,279
...will we stand against Esenbike?

719
01:06:47,720 --> 01:06:52,319
I see the one standing against me as
someone who has given up on their life.

720
01:06:55,560 --> 01:06:56,679
Altuga.

721
01:07:00,480 --> 01:07:01,719
But..

722
01:07:04,160 --> 01:07:05,279
For now..

723
01:07:05,840 --> 01:07:07,479
...we will do as she says.

724
01:07:09,520 --> 01:07:11,599
Get ready.

725
01:07:16,920 --> 01:07:19,839
Now...

726
01:07:19,840 --> 01:07:21,119
...it is time...

727
01:07:21,600 --> 01:07:23,639
...to drip blood from the swords.

728
01:07:32,840 --> 01:07:36,999
What are you saying, my Bey? That woman
lost her mind. That will never happen.

729
01:07:37,160 --> 01:07:38,679
My Fatma... No!

730
01:07:40,880 --> 01:07:44,439
My father told Esenbike the
same thing, mother. He said no.

731
01:07:44,440 --> 01:07:46,799
But that woman doesn't care, mother.

732
01:07:47,160 --> 01:07:50,199
She says "Either you will pay the tax, or...

733
01:07:53,040 --> 01:07:56,599
...I will take Fatma as a bride to my family."

734
01:07:58,080 --> 01:07:59,119
Father...

735
01:08:04,320 --> 01:08:05,359
Fatma.

736
01:08:11,640 --> 01:08:15,719
What is my brother saying, father?
Does Esenbike want me as a bride?

737
01:08:15,720 --> 01:08:20,479
Don't worry, my daughter, don't worry.
We have given the necessary answer.

738
01:08:22,960 --> 01:08:26,799
Even if you say no, what
if they take me by force?

739
01:08:27,000 --> 01:08:28,479
How can such a thing happen?

740
01:08:29,319 --> 01:08:29,719
Huh?

741
01:08:30,200 --> 01:08:33,158
Would I ever leave the
light of my eyes like that?

742
01:08:33,240 --> 01:08:34,759
No, don't worry.

743
01:08:36,479 --> 01:08:37,759
You won't leave me.

744
01:08:38,560 --> 01:08:39,919
You won't, right...

745
01:08:41,560 --> 01:08:44,359
If this woman is as strong as you say, Gonca...

746
01:08:47,319 --> 01:08:49,759
...when the time she gave us is up...

747
01:08:49,760 --> 01:08:53,839
When the time is up, we will
give the necessary answer.

748
01:08:55,160 --> 01:08:57,399
Children, inform the Beys.

749
01:08:57,920 --> 01:09:00,599
Let's discuss this matter in the council.

750
01:09:00,840 --> 01:09:03,479
-As you order my Bey.
-As you order my Bey.

751
01:09:11,840 --> 01:09:15,439
Let alone ruling a tribe...

752
01:09:17,399 --> 01:09:19,679
...you cannot even herd sheep.

753
01:09:24,359 --> 01:09:27,879
I entrusted my prisoner to you in your tribe.

754
01:09:28,200 --> 01:09:29,839
You couldn't keep him there.

755
01:09:32,000 --> 01:09:34,238
And without looking at your weakness...

756
01:09:35,040 --> 01:09:37,759
...you consider Osman your enemy.

757
01:09:39,680 --> 01:09:40,959
Esenbike Hatun...

758
01:09:41,640 --> 01:09:44,319
...there are more Nokers
than Alps in this tribe.

759
01:09:44,600 --> 01:09:48,559
If you are looking for someone
guilty, look at your own soldiers.

760
01:09:49,160 --> 01:09:50,759
Ilbay Bey is right.

761
01:09:51,240 --> 01:09:53,319
Apparently, Altuga helped him.

762
01:09:54,400 --> 01:09:56,639
Otherwise, he couldn't have escaped.

763
01:09:57,040 --> 01:10:01,359
Our Alps do not betray us.
They do not let criminals escape.

764
01:10:01,800 --> 01:10:04,719
Look for the traitors among yourselves.

765
01:10:09,760 --> 01:10:14,799
This situation of yours brings tears to my eyes.

766
01:10:16,480 --> 01:10:18,679
You support each other.

767
01:10:20,760 --> 01:10:21,799
Good.

768
01:10:25,840 --> 01:10:27,479
I care about the result.

769
01:10:29,760 --> 01:10:31,959
But I don't see Ulugan in the tribe.

770
01:10:33,160 --> 01:10:35,559
What is the result of the meeting then?

771
01:10:35,880 --> 01:10:38,319
Did Osman accept your conditions?

772
01:10:40,240 --> 01:10:44,559
He will. He will either accept...

773
01:10:48,160 --> 01:10:49,399
...or he will die.

774
01:10:52,240 --> 01:10:54,279
I gave Osman two days.

775
01:10:56,000 --> 01:10:58,719
He will both pay me taxes and...

776
01:11:01,120 --> 01:11:02,639
...give me his daughter.

777
01:11:13,079 --> 01:11:15,619
Osman Bey Secret Tents

778
01:11:17,840 --> 01:11:21,559
The fire inside me would
even heat the cold of this night.

779
01:11:25,120 --> 01:11:27,839
It is like I've been thrown into a blind well.

780
01:11:33,840 --> 01:11:35,839
This is the well of lovers, Yusuf.

781
01:11:35,880 --> 01:11:40,759
Those who are burnt to ashes and those who
can resist separation comes out of this well.

782
01:11:40,800 --> 01:11:43,439
In the name of Allah. Fatma Hatun.

783
01:11:46,720 --> 01:11:47,759
Are you alright?

784
01:11:49,120 --> 01:11:51,359
How can I be alright, Yusuf Bey?

785
01:11:52,840 --> 01:11:56,399
The Mongols have asked for me from my father.

786
01:11:57,840 --> 01:12:02,479
You must have heard about it, right? -I have.

787
01:12:02,960 --> 01:12:04,199
I have, I know.

788
01:12:05,360 --> 01:12:09,519
But it would be impossible to...

789
01:12:10,920 --> 01:12:16,479
...take a precious Hatun like you, I
mean the daughter of Osman Bey...

790
01:12:17,320 --> 01:12:18,719
...that's what I thought.

791
01:12:19,960 --> 01:12:21,719
My father won't give me to them.

792
01:12:23,440 --> 01:12:24,479
But what if...
-No.

793
01:12:25,400 --> 01:12:29,399
No, Fatma Hatun, there is no
such possibility. It's impossible.

794
01:12:29,680 --> 01:12:32,479
They will have to step over
my dead body to take you.

795
01:12:35,720 --> 01:12:36,759
I mean...

796
01:12:37,840 --> 01:12:39,159
...no one.

797
01:12:40,120 --> 01:12:45,039
...would want a girl who even makes
the sun jealous, a brave Turkish girl...

798
01:12:45,840 --> 01:12:51,359
...to rot in the hands of those Mongol dastards.

799
01:12:51,360 --> 01:12:53,639
I mean... that's what I think.

800
01:12:55,680 --> 01:12:57,359
Thank you, Yusuf Bey.

801
01:12:58,680 --> 01:13:03,359
But I'm afraid of their armies
coming here and attacking us.

802
01:13:11,160 --> 01:13:12,199
Meryem.

803
01:13:16,920 --> 01:13:20,239
Why are they here? -Meryem...

804
01:13:22,040 --> 01:13:23,319
Where are you going?

805
01:13:24,240 --> 01:13:25,479
I couldn't sleep.

806
01:13:26,120 --> 01:13:28,679
I thought I'd take some fresh air until suhoor.

807
01:13:28,680 --> 01:13:32,439
Meryem, it's very cold. You'll
catch a cold, you'll get sick.

808
01:13:34,160 --> 01:13:37,759
It's obvious I won't sleep tonight either.

809
01:13:38,640 --> 01:13:41,799
You'll be my companion. We'll talk, huh?

810
01:13:53,200 --> 01:13:56,599
Is there an army stronger
than your eyes, Fatma Hatun?

811
01:13:59,920 --> 01:14:02,519
Apparently, I won't sleep tonight either.

812
01:14:04,880 --> 01:14:05,919
God..

813
01:14:07,440 --> 01:14:10,399
Let us raise our child in health.

814
01:14:11,160 --> 01:14:14,119
Give us a good life to spend with him.

815
01:14:15,280 --> 01:14:20,879
Protect Orhan and our child from all evil.

816
01:14:32,160 --> 01:14:33,039
Amen.

817
01:15:16,880 --> 01:15:17,999
Holofira.

818
01:15:21,520 --> 01:15:22,999
My beautiful one...

819
01:15:25,200 --> 01:15:26,759
My beautiful wife...

820
01:15:27,400 --> 01:15:28,839
Why didn't you go to sleep?

821
01:15:28,840 --> 01:15:32,319
When have I ever slept without
your presence here, Shahzade Orhan?

822
01:15:32,320 --> 01:15:35,999
My wife, my spring flower.

823
01:15:36,360 --> 01:15:38,119
I know you won't sleep.

824
01:15:38,520 --> 01:15:43,039
But Holofira, you're carrying two lives now.

825
01:15:43,480 --> 01:15:47,719
You need to be careful
about eating and sleeping.

826
01:15:47,720 --> 01:15:54,799
-Look, my mother... She warned me.
-How does she do it?

827
01:15:56,120 --> 01:15:58,119
Being a mother to us all...

828
01:15:59,280 --> 01:16:03,559
Worrying for all of us... Loving all of us...

829
01:16:06,640 --> 01:16:09,999
I'm already afraid something
might happen to our baby.

830
01:16:12,120 --> 01:16:16,359
When I think that my mother
feels the same fear for all of us...

831
01:16:18,480 --> 01:16:19,519
Orhan.

832
01:16:21,400 --> 01:16:22,639
Do you think...

833
01:16:24,240 --> 01:16:26,199
...I will be a good mother?

834
01:16:27,720 --> 01:16:29,679
Sure you will.

835
01:16:30,160 --> 01:16:32,439
Sure you will. Lord's daughter.

836
01:16:34,840 --> 01:16:37,399
Are you sure?
-I am sure.

837
01:16:39,560 --> 01:16:42,879
Come here, come. Come.

838
01:16:43,480 --> 01:16:45,159
My Holofira

839
01:16:46,720 --> 01:16:47,759
Did..

840
01:16:52,960 --> 01:16:54,519
What did pregnancy do to me?

841
01:16:54,520 --> 01:16:58,523
I don't know. You
are just a little...

842
01:16:58,535 --> 01:17:00,079
A little what?

843
01:17:00,080 --> 01:17:04,199
I cannot say it but.. -Orhan! -Holofira...

844
01:17:04,440 --> 01:17:07,479
Look. Your hand is heavier now.

845
01:17:08,080 --> 01:17:09,679
My hand got heavier.

846
01:17:10,320 --> 01:17:12,959
I got heavier too, didn't I, Orhan Bey?

847
01:17:12,960 --> 01:17:16,119
My beautiful wife, my spring flower.

848
01:17:16,120 --> 01:17:23,479
Did I say that? I say pregnancy
added beauty to my wife's beauty.

849
01:17:23,720 --> 01:17:26,919
But you don't believe me, right?

850
01:17:27,960 --> 01:17:31,439
Then take this. Look at it.

851
01:17:38,880 --> 01:17:40,199
This is a lotus (Nilufer).

852
01:17:43,360 --> 01:17:45,239
Orhan, this is beautiful.

853
01:17:51,600 --> 01:17:54,159
-It's beautiful.
-It's beautiful.

854
01:17:55,000 --> 01:17:56,039
But...

855
01:17:57,760 --> 01:18:00,039
it's not as beautiful as you.

856
01:18:02,560 --> 01:18:04,439
Go to sleep now, alright?

857
01:18:04,480 --> 01:18:07,679
I'll perform my ablution and
read the Qur'an until suhoor.

858
01:18:07,680 --> 01:18:11,279
But you were going to read the Al-Kahf to me.

859
01:18:12,360 --> 01:18:15,079
And you were going to explain what it means.

860
01:18:15,080 --> 01:18:16,559
Don't think I forgot.

861
01:18:16,560 --> 01:18:19,839
You just don't want to go to sleep...
-I would never.

862
01:18:25,720 --> 01:18:28,679
Do I need to perform ablution to listen?

863
01:18:29,880 --> 01:18:33,519
You don't need to, my Hatun.

864
01:18:36,720 --> 01:18:37,879
Come here.

865
01:18:39,200 --> 01:18:40,599
My beautiful Hatun.

866
01:19:03,720 --> 01:19:07,239
-Did she speak?
-She won't speak.

867
01:19:09,040 --> 01:19:12,919
I want that snake to be
punished more than you, Osman.

868
01:19:13,920 --> 01:19:15,199
But what about Halime?

869
01:19:16,160 --> 01:19:17,319
Our daughter?

870
01:19:19,520 --> 01:19:21,839
Who knows what she's doing right now?

871
01:19:26,320 --> 01:19:28,039
The Mongols are right here.

872
01:19:29,200 --> 01:19:31,639
Our people are in a miserable situation.

873
01:19:32,280 --> 01:19:36,519
The fate of our daughter is in
the hands of that poisonous snake.

874
01:19:40,160 --> 01:19:44,599
If we keep Sofia alive, there's
hope to reunite with our daughter.

875
01:19:45,920 --> 01:19:47,599
But what if she doesn't speak?

876
01:19:48,440 --> 01:19:52,319
What if she continues her game?
Are we going to be her prisoners then?

877
01:19:52,320 --> 01:19:53,999
My Bala, don't.

878
01:19:54,520 --> 01:19:58,519
Don't, my gazelle-eyed
one. Don't shed your tears.

879
01:19:59,480 --> 01:20:06,119
Look, my Halime is alive. You
see. We'll find her. We'll take her.

880
01:20:06,200 --> 01:20:08,079
We'll take her and the tribe.

881
01:20:09,600 --> 01:20:12,559
Don't cry, don't shed these beautiful tears.

882
01:20:15,280 --> 01:20:18,039
We got over many hardships until now.

883
01:20:18,400 --> 01:20:22,479
We will get over this too. Don't worry.

884
01:20:22,480 --> 01:20:26,519
We'll find her, Osman. We
will win this battle, God willing.

885
01:20:26,880 --> 01:20:31,599
Did I ever lose something
when I had you by my side?

886
01:20:32,240 --> 01:20:34,359
You'll see, all ways will open before us.

887
01:20:39,040 --> 01:20:44,199
When I close my eyes, her face comes before me.

888
01:20:49,120 --> 01:20:52,759
She's crying out for her mother.

889
01:20:55,720 --> 01:20:59,159
Who knows what that demon did to our daughter?

890
01:21:00,160 --> 01:21:02,999
-What did our daughter suffer?
-Hush.

891
01:21:03,480 --> 01:21:06,439
No, no.

892
01:21:06,720 --> 01:21:08,919
We'll think about the good days...

893
01:21:09,880 --> 01:21:11,999
...not the days we lost.

894
01:21:12,240 --> 01:21:13,959
Alright?

895
01:21:17,600 --> 01:21:20,679
What if she doesn't
remember us when we find her?

896
01:21:23,520 --> 01:21:27,039
Even if our daughter doesn't remember her mother

897
01:21:27,680 --> 01:21:31,159
...her mother raised her right here.

898
01:21:33,080 --> 01:21:35,839
-Here.
-Yes.

899
01:21:37,640 --> 01:21:40,679
You saved me from my burden again, my Osman.

900
01:21:45,320 --> 01:21:49,639
Without you, what could I count on?

901
01:21:51,120 --> 01:21:54,799
I'm your protector. You are my companion.

902
01:21:57,680 --> 01:21:59,919
I'll fight any battles with you.

903
01:22:00,880 --> 01:22:04,839
You say we'll end this battle happily?

904
01:22:06,720 --> 01:22:09,359
We will win this battle too.

905
01:22:38,720 --> 01:22:40,119
Again?

906
01:22:44,320 --> 01:22:46,599
I told you to wait in the tent.

907
01:22:46,760 --> 01:22:50,679
-Father, well...
-You may catch cold, Aykiz.

908
01:22:52,120 --> 01:22:53,959
Take her to the tent.

909
01:23:08,240 --> 01:23:09,479
We're under attack!

910
01:23:09,480 --> 01:23:11,279
-Father.
-Stay in the tent.

911
01:23:27,320 --> 01:23:30,999
Leave no heads over the shoulders! Attack!

912
01:23:54,080 --> 01:23:57,959
Get your bloody hands off my tribe, dog!

913
01:24:09,360 --> 01:24:14,719
I burned down the tribes all night.

914
01:24:16,000 --> 01:24:21,479
Now you're going to burn with your tribe.

915
01:24:38,000 --> 01:24:39,599
Burn down!

916
01:24:40,040 --> 01:24:44,239
Burn down their tents and tribe!

917
01:24:50,680 --> 01:24:54,799
We've been burning the tribes
who pledged loyalty to Osman.

918
01:24:55,240 --> 01:24:57,279
They'll wake up into a nightmare.

919
01:24:57,400 --> 01:25:02,799
I'll make them wish they were dead, Altuga!

920
01:25:04,120 --> 01:25:07,119
Osman Bey Secret Tents

921
01:25:07,520 --> 01:25:11,959
They all know we won't kneel.

922
01:25:12,760 --> 01:25:16,199
So she set a condition to make us kneel.

923
01:25:16,360 --> 01:25:20,679
Although Ayaz Bey and his alps joined us,

924
01:25:21,240 --> 01:25:26,479
...we still can't drive Esenbike
out of the frontiers, my Bey.

925
01:25:28,160 --> 01:25:30,319
Orhan Bey is right.

926
01:25:31,240 --> 01:25:36,359
To become more powerful
for more alps and swords.

927
01:25:37,600 --> 01:25:39,759
...we need money.

928
01:25:41,120 --> 01:25:42,879
Well..

929
01:25:43,160 --> 01:25:48,919
The enemies know that they can
put us in a tight spot with money.

930
01:25:51,720 --> 01:25:56,719
But we have to find the money
to stand against Mongolians.

931
01:25:57,000 --> 01:25:59,599
Well... My Bey.

932
01:26:02,160 --> 01:26:06,959
It's not just little money. How can we find it?

933
01:26:10,240 --> 01:26:12,439
With the money of Mongolians.

934
01:26:13,720 --> 01:26:15,359
Don't worry, son.

935
01:26:15,600 --> 01:26:18,759
We'll hit Mongolians with
the money of Mongolians.

936
01:26:23,400 --> 01:26:25,239
Do I have permission, my Bey?

937
01:26:25,960 --> 01:26:27,759
Come in, Aykurt.

938
01:26:29,400 --> 01:26:30,759
My Bey

939
01:26:31,160 --> 01:26:35,599
The dog called Ulugan
raided all the Turkmen tribes.

940
01:26:35,840 --> 01:26:37,999
He slaughtered people, my Bey.

941
01:26:38,880 --> 01:26:41,159
What are you saying, Aykurt Cavus?

942
01:27:04,360 --> 01:27:06,519
She said nothing, Bala Hatun.

943
01:27:10,040 --> 01:27:11,799
Sofia.

944
01:27:16,400 --> 01:27:18,839
I never give up, Bala.

945
01:27:21,640 --> 01:27:25,319
For years, I waited for vengeance.

946
01:27:27,760 --> 01:27:31,679
And you think I will give up so easily?

947
01:27:33,160 --> 01:27:36,639
If not today, you will give up tomorrow.

948
01:27:37,360 --> 01:27:39,279
Beat her hard, Kismet.

949
01:27:39,560 --> 01:27:43,039
You'll speak. I can wait, Sofia.

950
01:27:44,000 --> 01:27:46,759
But Halime can't wait, Bala.

951
01:27:48,240 --> 01:27:50,319
She doesn't have much time.

952
01:27:50,960 --> 01:27:52,599
What do you mean?

953
01:27:52,880 --> 01:27:54,239
Bala.

954
01:27:54,880 --> 01:27:57,479
You have to release me.

955
01:27:58,000 --> 01:27:59,559
For Halime.

956
01:28:03,280 --> 01:28:05,079
Sofia!

957
01:28:05,920 --> 01:28:07,479
Game is over, Sofia.

958
01:28:07,560 --> 01:28:10,679
Whatever you say, you won't get out of here.

959
01:28:10,680 --> 01:28:13,599
Look, Bala.

960
01:28:14,960 --> 01:28:18,359
If you don't let me go,
Halime will die tomorrow.

961
01:28:18,400 --> 01:28:19,548
What?

962
01:28:19,560 --> 01:28:23,039
My soldiers must have
realized my absence, Bala.

963
01:28:25,760 --> 01:28:29,119
"Three days if Osman
catches me", I said to them.

964
01:28:32,360 --> 01:28:34,039
If I don't go back in three days,

965
01:28:36,040 --> 01:28:37,999
...they will kill Halime.

966
01:28:42,120 --> 01:28:45,479
Whatever you say! I'm sick of your lies!

967
01:28:45,760 --> 01:28:49,159
-I'm sick of you!
-It's real.

968
01:28:51,920 --> 01:28:54,599
I'm telling the truth.

969
01:28:56,240 --> 01:28:59,359
I swear to God that it's the truth, Bala.

970
01:29:01,240 --> 01:29:04,039
If you don't want her to be killed.

971
01:29:08,800 --> 01:29:11,039
...you have to release me.

972
01:29:13,480 --> 01:29:17,399
Otherwise, she'll die tomorrow.

973
01:29:17,960 --> 01:29:21,279
You'll cause your daughter to die.

974
01:29:21,840 --> 01:29:24,319
Just let me go.

975
01:29:30,960 --> 01:29:33,119
We don't have much time, Bala.

976
01:29:52,520 --> 01:29:54,559
Ulugan, Ulugan.

977
01:29:55,200 --> 01:29:58,079
You rabid dog attacking around.

978
01:29:58,880 --> 01:30:01,239
As soon as he ran away from Esenbike

979
01:30:01,400 --> 01:30:04,199
...he attacked innocent Turks.

980
01:30:04,360 --> 01:30:09,559
It's us who caused him to lose
favor with Olcaytu, Alaaddin Bey.

981
01:30:09,840 --> 01:30:13,839
Ulugan's grudge and hatred...

982
01:30:14,120 --> 01:30:17,479
...is against us more than our people.

983
01:30:20,720 --> 01:30:24,319
Maybe, it's not about only his
hatred against us, my Shahzade.

984
01:30:24,880 --> 01:30:26,879
You're right, brother.

985
01:30:27,960 --> 01:30:29,199
My Bey.

986
01:30:29,520 --> 01:30:31,199
We heard Esenbike.

987
01:30:31,640 --> 01:30:36,599
What if Ulugan is trying to
prevent the peace as she said?

988
01:30:38,840 --> 01:30:43,239
Even if find the gold now, my Bey

989
01:30:43,800 --> 01:30:49,919
...we can't fight both Ulugan and
Esenbike in two fronts at the same time.

990
01:30:52,400 --> 01:30:58,159
My Bey, I know what they call peace
requires us to kneel and pay taxes.

991
01:30:58,920 --> 01:31:01,559
But...
-No.

992
01:31:02,400 --> 01:31:05,039
With Ulugan's new move

993
01:31:07,320 --> 01:31:09,799
...things have changed.

994
01:31:12,240 --> 01:31:16,239
Beys, there is nothing to do.

995
01:31:19,080 --> 01:31:21,439
We will pay the tax to Mongolians.

996
01:31:25,800 --> 01:31:30,799
The Mongolian gold that we were going to use
to drive Esenbike out of the frontiers...

997
01:31:33,280 --> 01:31:36,039
We'll pay it to Mongolians as the tax.

998
01:31:38,600 --> 01:31:40,639
I'm standing by my word.

999
01:31:42,200 --> 01:31:48,279
Not a single coin from the treasure of
my people's pouches will go to them.

1000
01:31:49,480 --> 01:31:56,159
Esenbike will think that
we made peace and knelt.

1001
01:31:57,880 --> 01:32:03,159
In fact, we will buy time to choke them.

1002
01:32:08,600 --> 01:32:12,999
How will we get the Mongolian gold, my Bey.
-Well...

1003
01:32:13,760 --> 01:32:16,599
Here is the answer of that question.

1004
01:32:17,160 --> 01:32:21,279
Samil, Balaban, Kanyumaz.

1005
01:32:24,320 --> 01:32:27,719
They've been watching
Ulugan's nokers. Speak now.

1006
01:32:28,200 --> 01:32:29,879
As you order, my Bey.

1007
01:32:30,200 --> 01:32:34,919
As Osman Bey said, we've been
watching their every step for some time.

1008
01:32:35,400 --> 01:32:37,639
Before Esenbike came to the frontiers

1009
01:32:37,720 --> 01:32:41,599
...carts loaded with gold would come
to Ulugan from the nearby beylics.

1010
01:32:41,760 --> 01:32:42,919
What's the load?

1011
01:32:42,920 --> 01:32:46,759
The taxes collected beyond the
eastern border of Kayi, Ulugan.

1012
01:32:48,000 --> 01:32:52,679
Altuga, put these beside the others. Come on.

1013
01:32:54,200 --> 01:32:57,839
Thinking where they could
keep the gold, we followed them.

1014
01:32:59,120 --> 01:33:01,199
Come on, carry the chests.

1015
01:33:01,440 --> 01:33:03,559
Hide them well in the cave.

1016
01:33:07,200 --> 01:33:10,399
They dropped the chest in front of our eyes.

1017
01:33:10,520 --> 01:33:12,799
What are you doing?

1018
01:33:17,000 --> 01:33:19,079
All the gold coins fell on the ground.

1019
01:33:19,520 --> 01:33:24,039
Allah knows how much more
they are keeping in that cave.

1020
01:33:25,720 --> 01:33:29,359
My Bey, that's why they're
providing tight security.

1021
01:33:35,680 --> 01:33:38,119
Kanyumaz, what you saying is...

1022
01:33:39,480 --> 01:33:40,679
My Bey.

1023
01:33:40,840 --> 01:33:45,239
Your plan is taking Ulugan's gold...

1024
01:33:45,640 --> 01:33:48,439
...and giving it to Esenbike as the tax, huh?

1025
01:33:48,640 --> 01:33:54,759
This will be enough to buy time
until we regain our strength, my Bey.

1026
01:33:56,520 --> 01:33:58,599
Esenbike..

1027
01:33:59,880 --> 01:34:04,159
...will think I have to accept the peace.

1028
01:34:05,400 --> 01:34:07,199
But we'll regain strength.

1029
01:34:07,520 --> 01:34:11,639
First, we will kill Ulugan and then...

1030
01:34:12,760 --> 01:34:15,919
...and then stop Esenbike.

1031
01:34:22,000 --> 01:34:23,759
Here we go.

1032
01:34:24,480 --> 01:34:26,719
Let's pay a visit to that cave.

1033
01:35:40,840 --> 01:35:42,479
My mother Sultan.

1034
01:35:43,240 --> 01:35:45,359
Shah of Shahs.

1035
01:35:47,960 --> 01:35:52,239
You didn't think anyone
was worthy of your precious.

1036
01:35:52,600 --> 01:35:57,639
But you prepared so much
for a shepherd's daughter.

1037
01:35:58,320 --> 01:36:01,919
It means there is a great benefit for us.

1038
01:36:06,760 --> 01:36:12,999
This is a great chance for you to
prove that you're a grandchild worthy...

1039
01:36:13,720 --> 01:36:16,039
...of Olcaytu Khan, my boy.

1040
01:36:30,280 --> 01:36:34,479
My Sultan, Ulugan carried out your orders.

1041
01:36:34,760 --> 01:36:39,159
He raided all the nearby
tribes and slaughtered people.

1042
01:36:39,480 --> 01:36:41,439
He seized their everything.

1043
01:36:45,480 --> 01:36:49,719
Good. Good.

1044
01:36:51,360 --> 01:36:52,959
Now..

1045
01:36:53,360 --> 01:36:56,439
...you're trapped, Osman.

1046
01:36:58,440 --> 01:37:05,679
Still, he will look around
for the tax you ordered.

1047
01:37:08,080 --> 01:37:12,759
He'll come back with empty
hands from everywhere.

1048
01:37:13,560 --> 01:37:18,559
We have all the treasures...

1049
01:37:19,520 --> 01:37:23,519
...of the tribes, Sogut and all the castles.

1050
01:37:25,400 --> 01:37:30,479
But Osman will try something.

1051
01:37:34,320 --> 01:37:37,199
He will attempt to take back...

1052
01:37:38,080 --> 01:37:40,079
..what we took from him.

1053
01:37:40,240 --> 01:37:45,119
He'll come for the Mongolian
treasure that we're keeping in the cave.

1054
01:37:50,400 --> 01:37:53,439
There, he will face Altuga.

1055
01:37:54,040 --> 01:37:58,479
While Osman thinks he'll get the treasure,

1056
01:38:00,120 --> 01:38:02,559
...he'll fall into our net, huh?

1057
01:38:03,040 --> 01:38:04,799
Mother Sultan.

1058
01:38:05,400 --> 01:38:07,799
You've started to wind around.

1059
01:38:17,440 --> 01:38:19,519
Not wind.

1060
01:38:20,840 --> 01:38:23,079
I'll storm around!

1061
01:38:26,080 --> 01:38:28,359
Osman will get ruined...

1062
01:38:28,680 --> 01:38:32,999
...and lose his leaves one by one.

1063
01:38:39,840 --> 01:38:44,159
Osman is running into the death clutch.

1064
01:38:44,760 --> 01:38:48,239
We'll wait until they are trapped, nokers.

1065
01:38:48,520 --> 01:38:52,519
The journey they started
for the gold will be their grave.

1066
01:38:53,440 --> 01:38:58,359
Osman, your poor mind...

1067
01:39:00,000 --> 01:39:02,759
...will let you down this time.

1068
01:39:25,280 --> 01:39:27,359
What if she is telling the truth?

1069
01:39:27,400 --> 01:39:30,119
What if they really kill my Halime tomorrow?

1070
01:39:35,480 --> 01:39:36,519
No...

1071
01:39:36,680 --> 01:39:39,639
No, I have to do something.
-Don't, mother.

1072
01:39:40,120 --> 01:39:44,079
We cannot trust the word of that snake Sofia.
-We don't have time.

1073
01:39:44,200 --> 01:39:45,239
Three days.

1074
01:39:45,320 --> 01:39:49,199
She says they will kill Halime if
she doesn't go there in three days.

1075
01:39:49,840 --> 01:39:52,279
What if it's too late tomorrow, Gonca?

1076
01:39:53,120 --> 01:39:55,559
Mother, Sofia is doing this to be set free.

1077
01:39:55,560 --> 01:39:57,559
That traitor can do anything for that.

1078
01:39:57,600 --> 01:39:59,119
She is playing with your pain.

1079
01:40:01,080 --> 01:40:04,839
Mother, we cannot trust her.
-But...

1080
01:40:05,760 --> 01:40:07,679
...what if Sofia is telling the truth?

1081
01:40:08,400 --> 01:40:10,439
What if they really kill her?

1082
01:40:12,280 --> 01:40:14,319
I lost my daughter once.

1083
01:40:14,840 --> 01:40:16,319
I experienced that grief.

1084
01:40:16,840 --> 01:40:18,799
I cannot resist losing her again...

1085
01:40:19,280 --> 01:40:21,599
...without coming together with her.

1086
01:40:23,520 --> 01:40:25,319
We won't lose her, mother.

1087
01:40:25,400 --> 01:40:27,519
We will come together with my sister.

1088
01:40:27,520 --> 01:40:30,119
But that snake Sofia is lying.

1089
01:40:30,800 --> 01:40:33,679
She couldn't have known
that she would get caught.

1090
01:40:34,320 --> 01:40:35,359
Mother..

1091
01:40:36,240 --> 01:40:37,759
Let's just wait for my father.

1092
01:41:04,720 --> 01:41:06,039
Come here.

1093
01:41:07,840 --> 01:41:08,879
My Bey.

1094
01:41:09,160 --> 01:41:12,719
The cave where they have
hidden the treasure is just ahead.

1095
01:41:13,600 --> 01:41:18,039
Now, they must have taken all kinds
of measures to protect the gold, my Bey.

1096
01:41:18,480 --> 01:41:19,999
Okay, okay.

1097
01:41:20,160 --> 01:41:23,719
Now there will be too many
nokers at the place we will go.

1098
01:41:24,080 --> 01:41:26,519
We will kill them all. If...

1099
01:41:26,640 --> 01:41:29,159
...any of them survives...

1100
01:41:29,760 --> 01:41:32,079
...then we will pay a heavy price. Know that.

1101
01:41:32,280 --> 01:41:33,999
As you order my Bey.

1102
01:41:34,560 --> 01:41:35,759
Come on now.

1103
01:41:36,080 --> 01:41:38,959
We will go to the cave
on foot. Draw your swords.

1104
01:41:43,120 --> 01:41:44,199
Okay.

1105
01:41:58,440 --> 01:42:00,239
Osman is coming Altuga.

1106
01:42:01,120 --> 01:42:02,319
Let him come.

1107
01:42:03,040 --> 01:42:04,399
Let him come.

1108
01:42:04,920 --> 01:42:07,199
Get ready to shed blood Nokers.

1109
01:42:07,800 --> 01:42:09,359
Our prey is approaching us.

1110
01:42:09,360 --> 01:42:11,279
Everyone take cover, come on!

1111
01:42:13,840 --> 01:42:14,879
Come on!

1112
01:42:38,800 --> 01:42:41,159
Did you make your decision, Bala?

1113
01:42:43,800 --> 01:42:48,159
You lost your daughter once. You
don't want to lose her again, right?

1114
01:42:55,360 --> 01:42:57,519
You will take me to my daughter, Sofia.

1115
01:43:06,840 --> 01:43:08,799
It's not that easy, Bala.

1116
01:43:13,560 --> 01:43:16,759
Why would you let me live
after taking your daughter?

1117
01:43:19,360 --> 01:43:21,959
I have to be sure that...

1118
01:43:22,640 --> 01:43:24,399
...you won't kill me.

1119
01:43:25,000 --> 01:43:28,519
We will get out of here
secretly. Just you and me.

1120
01:43:32,640 --> 01:43:34,679
If I don't have swords...

1121
01:43:37,240 --> 01:43:38,919
...you won't have any either.

1122
01:43:49,280 --> 01:43:50,319
Good.

1123
01:43:50,480 --> 01:43:52,039
I won't take my sword with me.

1124
01:43:52,720 --> 01:43:55,359
I will put it here while we are leaving.

1125
01:43:55,440 --> 01:43:57,519
You will take me to my daughter.

1126
01:43:58,120 --> 01:44:00,879
And I won't take your
dirty life and I will let you go.

1127
01:44:00,920 --> 01:44:02,159
This is our deal.

1128
01:44:03,520 --> 01:44:05,759
I will do this for my Halime, Sofia.

1129
01:44:08,840 --> 01:44:10,719
Come on. Get

1130
01:44:11,520 --> 01:44:12,559
Get up

1131
01:44:18,200 --> 01:44:19,879
I gave Alps duties.

1132
01:44:19,960 --> 01:44:22,119
We will leave before they return.

1133
01:44:27,800 --> 01:44:28,839
Walk!

1134
01:44:34,320 --> 01:44:36,199
Walk!

1135
01:44:40,110 --> 01:44:42,499
Near Osman Bey Secret Tents

1136
01:44:42,580 --> 01:44:44,659
So you took refuge here, huh?

1137
01:44:46,160 --> 01:44:48,239
But you cannot run away from Ulugan.

1138
01:44:49,520 --> 01:44:50,919
I found you.

1139
01:44:54,520 --> 01:44:55,559
Come on!

1140
01:44:59,160 --> 01:45:00,199
Walk!

1141
01:45:03,160 --> 01:45:05,279
Walk, you snake, walk!

1142
01:45:07,960 --> 01:45:11,039
We have to leave before Alps return. Come on!

1143
01:45:11,120 --> 01:45:13,719
Come on! You will take me to my daughter!

1144
01:45:15,400 --> 01:45:16,439
Walk!

1145
01:45:17,800 --> 01:45:18,839
Come on!

1146
01:45:19,360 --> 01:45:21,519
Walk!

1147
01:45:22,600 --> 01:45:24,439
Wait.

1148
01:45:31,120 --> 01:45:34,239
Move Sofia.

1149
01:45:40,880 --> 01:45:41,919
Come on.

1150
01:45:44,320 --> 01:45:45,359
Walk!

1151
01:45:49,240 --> 01:45:50,799
Come on, walk, Sofia!

1152
01:46:03,280 --> 01:46:05,799
From here on, we will be careful.

1153
01:46:06,680 --> 01:46:08,519
We will move more quietly.

1154
01:46:14,200 --> 01:46:15,239
Stop!

1155
01:46:44,320 --> 01:46:46,839
Be careful.

1156
01:46:47,360 --> 01:46:48,399
As you see..

1157
01:46:48,920 --> 01:46:50,279
...there are traps here.

1158
01:46:50,400 --> 01:46:51,839
Thank you Osman Bey.

1159
01:46:52,480 --> 01:46:55,199
Everyone should be careful where they step.

1160
01:46:55,360 --> 01:46:59,079
Those dogs set traps everywhere.
-Come on.

1161
01:47:00,160 --> 01:47:01,519
Prepare the arrows.

1162
01:47:25,000 --> 01:47:27,519
Alps... prepare your bows.

1163
01:47:27,520 --> 01:47:31,079
As you order, my Bey.
-Shoot your arrows.

1164
01:47:38,080 --> 01:47:39,839
Come on now.

1165
01:47:55,920 --> 01:47:57,119
Osman.

1166
01:47:57,840 --> 01:47:59,159
Osman and..

1167
01:48:00,080 --> 01:48:01,999
...his low companions.

1168
01:48:03,400 --> 01:48:04,519
What happened?

1169
01:48:04,760 --> 01:48:06,679
You seem shocked.

1170
01:48:08,040 --> 01:48:13,719
Did you really think we would just
leave our treasure to you like that?

1171
01:48:14,160 --> 01:48:16,039
This is...

1172
01:48:16,440 --> 01:48:18,279
...the end of the way for you, Altuga.

1173
01:48:19,200 --> 01:48:21,399
Turn back from the path you have taken.

1174
01:48:21,400 --> 01:48:22,479
Altuga...

1175
01:48:23,640 --> 01:48:25,239
As Cerkutay said...

1176
01:48:26,440 --> 01:48:27,279
Come on.

1177
01:48:28,560 --> 01:48:31,599
Ask for forgiveness when
you still have the chance.

1178
01:48:31,720 --> 01:48:33,399
Accept Islam.

1179
01:48:37,000 --> 01:48:38,199
Accept it...

1180
01:48:40,960 --> 01:48:42,199
...so I will forgive you.

1181
01:48:48,080 --> 01:48:49,599
I will never give up.

1182
01:48:51,280 --> 01:48:52,879
Keep your faith to yourself.

1183
01:49:03,320 --> 01:49:04,439
Then..

1184
01:49:06,720 --> 01:49:08,039
...you will die.

1185
01:49:08,880 --> 01:49:10,319
You cannot decide...

1186
01:49:10,640 --> 01:49:13,799
...who will die and who will live, Osman.

1187
01:49:15,080 --> 01:49:16,239
Nokers!

1188
01:49:27,120 --> 01:49:29,879
You left us no choice then.

1189
01:49:30,480 --> 01:49:32,639
-Attack!
-Attack!

1190
01:50:37,000 --> 01:50:39,839
Come on valiants! Kill them!

1191
01:50:53,160 --> 01:50:55,868
Even if I thought for
years, I never would have

1192
01:50:55,880 --> 01:50:58,599
imagined that you would
be my savior angel Bala.

1193
01:51:03,120 --> 01:51:04,159
You..

1194
01:51:04,640 --> 01:51:08,839
...you took me out of your tribe huh?

1195
01:51:18,080 --> 01:51:20,079
Do not test my patience, Sofia.

1196
01:51:20,200 --> 01:51:22,239
Just tell me which way we will go.

1197
01:51:23,600 --> 01:51:26,359
To my daughter. To your Halime.

1198
01:51:27,720 --> 01:51:28,759
She is not your..

1199
01:51:29,600 --> 01:51:33,239
Let me tell you again...

1200
01:51:35,680 --> 01:51:37,479
She is not your Halime anymore.

1201
01:51:37,480 --> 01:51:39,199
She is a true Christian.

1202
01:51:40,560 --> 01:51:42,839
And she hates Turks!

1203
01:51:44,400 --> 01:51:47,159
Because I raised her. -Sofia!

1204
01:51:48,680 --> 01:51:51,079
I will cleanse my child from your poison.

1205
01:51:51,280 --> 01:51:53,719
I will set you free for my daughter today.

1206
01:51:53,720 --> 01:51:57,559
But I swear, I will never give up on my revenge.

1207
01:51:58,520 --> 01:51:59,559
Walk!

1208
01:52:01,560 --> 01:52:03,399
Walk!

1209
01:52:06,560 --> 01:52:08,559
Your daughter, huh?

1210
01:52:20,720 --> 01:52:22,079
Can I come in?

1211
01:52:23,760 --> 01:52:24,799
Come in.

1212
01:52:38,640 --> 01:52:39,839
Esenbike Hatun.

1213
01:52:40,600 --> 01:52:42,119
I have important news.

1214
01:52:43,760 --> 01:52:46,759
Tell me, I will decide
if it is important or not.

1215
01:52:47,400 --> 01:52:48,439
Sofia.

1216
01:52:49,040 --> 01:52:51,439
She is an important person for Byzantine.

1217
01:52:51,640 --> 01:52:56,759
She is Ulugan's and our ally.
-So? -Osman captured her.

1218
01:52:57,200 --> 01:53:01,359
He has our strongest ally. Give them orders...
-You insolent man!

1219
01:53:03,680 --> 01:53:06,519
Who are you to advise me?

1220
01:53:12,600 --> 01:53:14,999
And they say Kayis are smart.

1221
01:53:16,920 --> 01:53:19,159
Who did you take after, Ilbay?

1222
01:53:21,400 --> 01:53:24,119
What did I tell you when I came here?

1223
01:53:24,920 --> 01:53:26,879
Sorry, Esenbike Hatun.

1224
01:53:27,720 --> 01:53:29,279
If we save her, we can...

1225
01:53:29,279 --> 01:53:30,919
I don't have allies!

1226
01:53:32,880 --> 01:53:34,329
I have servants!

1227
01:53:39,600 --> 01:53:40,639
Get lost!

1228
01:53:42,040 --> 01:53:44,039
You've wasted my time enough!

1229
01:54:29,480 --> 01:54:31,319
Die, brother.

1230
01:54:44,000 --> 01:54:46,439
Cerkutay, now go and take your revenge.

1231
01:54:46,440 --> 01:54:50,199
Thank you my Bey.

1232
01:54:55,800 --> 01:54:58,319
Shame on the efforts I made for you, Altuga.

1233
01:54:58,720 --> 01:55:00,359
Don't you have a heart?

1234
01:55:01,120 --> 01:55:02,599
How can you do this to us?

1235
01:55:02,800 --> 01:55:06,999
Stop speaking, let your sword speak, brother.

1236
01:55:07,800 --> 01:55:09,399
I will be silent now.

1237
01:55:11,000 --> 01:55:13,479
But my swords will never remain silent.

1238
01:55:35,960 --> 01:55:38,159
How much farther do we have to go, Sofia?

1239
01:55:38,240 --> 01:55:41,759
Do you think I don't know that
Byzantine patrols are placed here?

1240
01:55:45,880 --> 01:55:46,919
But..

1241
01:55:47,200 --> 01:55:49,159
...we will go this way.

1242
01:55:50,760 --> 01:55:52,719
Soldiers don't come here.

1243
01:55:54,080 --> 01:55:55,119
Then..

1244
01:55:56,360 --> 01:55:57,999
...after we get out of the forest...

1245
01:55:58,400 --> 01:56:02,959
...we will arrive in a hidden
Christian village in a secret city.

1246
01:56:04,320 --> 01:56:05,759
Your daughter is there.

1247
01:56:07,880 --> 01:56:09,399
My Halime is there, huh?

1248
01:56:10,400 --> 01:56:11,439
Bala.

1249
01:56:13,760 --> 01:56:15,439
Aren't you afraid, huh?

1250
01:56:17,280 --> 01:56:22,079
Aren't you afraid that I will kill you when
you take your daughter and set me free?

1251
01:56:22,440 --> 01:56:25,359
I risked everything for my daughter, Sofia.

1252
01:56:25,840 --> 01:56:27,919
I made an agreement with a snake.

1253
01:56:32,640 --> 01:56:33,679
With you.

1254
01:56:35,440 --> 01:56:38,399
I saved my enemy from captivity.

1255
01:56:38,760 --> 01:56:42,719
Think about what I can do
for my daughter. And fear.

1256
01:56:43,520 --> 01:56:45,119
There is no time to wait.

1257
01:56:45,560 --> 01:56:47,719
I will take Sofia out of the tribe.

1258
01:56:47,760 --> 01:56:49,599
Only I will go with her.

1259
01:56:50,360 --> 01:56:52,039
She will take me to Halime.

1260
01:56:52,040 --> 01:56:54,710
Mother, that snake
is setting a trap.

1261
01:56:54,722 --> 01:56:55,639
Sure she is!

1262
01:56:55,760 --> 01:56:58,239
But we will set a trap against her as well.

1263
01:56:58,240 --> 01:57:03,359
You will take Gonca and
Alps and follow us secretly.

1264
01:57:03,360 --> 01:57:05,279
You don't have to be afraid, Bala.

1265
01:57:05,920 --> 01:57:09,959
We made an agreement. And we
will stay loyal to that agreement, right?

1266
01:57:12,120 --> 01:57:13,879
Come on.

1267
01:57:15,840 --> 01:57:17,039
Sofia.

1268
01:57:17,320 --> 01:57:22,119
If we don't arrive before my
soldiers, your daughter will die.

1269
01:57:27,600 --> 01:57:29,199
Come on!

1270
01:57:29,720 --> 01:57:31,199
Move.

1271
01:57:33,040 --> 01:57:34,479
Move.

1272
01:57:35,520 --> 01:57:36,719
Alaaddin.

1273
01:57:37,200 --> 01:57:41,079
-We should get closer. We may lose them.

1274
01:57:41,440 --> 01:57:44,919
Just in case, Gonca. We
shouldn't draw suspicion.

1275
01:57:45,280 --> 01:57:47,639
That snake can do anything.

1276
01:57:47,840 --> 01:57:49,999
We will keep tracking from a distance.

1277
01:57:57,280 --> 01:57:59,519
Alps, stand ready!

1278
01:58:02,240 --> 01:58:05,319
Master Sofia thanks you for hosting her.

1279
01:58:06,640 --> 01:58:09,039
You vile dogs.

1280
01:58:29,360 --> 01:58:31,759
Allah is the greatest!

1281
01:58:44,320 --> 01:58:47,399
Nokers, we're drawing back to the cave!

1282
01:58:48,880 --> 01:58:52,399
-Nokers!
-Cerkutay, are you alright?

1283
01:58:52,560 --> 01:58:54,319
I'm fine.

1284
01:58:54,880 --> 01:58:56,719
Alright

1285
01:59:04,480 --> 01:59:08,159
-Come here, Osman.
-Where are you going, dog?

1286
01:59:08,600 --> 01:59:10,919
Just wait.

1287
01:59:11,520 --> 01:59:13,159
Osman.

1288
01:59:14,080 --> 01:59:18,919
I thought your mind was working
like a wolf's mind. But I was wrong.

1289
01:59:19,760 --> 01:59:23,239
It was just to stall you.

1290
01:59:24,760 --> 01:59:27,279
What are you talking about, dastard?

1291
01:59:27,800 --> 01:59:29,959
Easy, fiery boy.

1292
01:59:30,400 --> 01:59:33,479
I'm saying... While you're after the gold here,

1293
01:59:34,160 --> 01:59:37,679
...Ulugan has gone to raid your secret tribe.

1294
01:59:37,760 --> 01:59:39,559
What?

1295
01:59:40,200 --> 01:59:42,879
-Dastards.
-Cerkutay.

1296
01:59:42,920 --> 01:59:47,119
Don't do it. Don't.

1297
01:59:51,160 --> 01:59:55,319
Otherwise, we'll all burn. All of us.

1298
01:59:56,240 --> 02:00:01,919
But today it's not me but you who will burn.

1299
02:00:12,960 --> 02:00:15,479
Good bye, brother.

1300
02:00:17,880 --> 02:00:20,559
-Alps!
My Bey.

1301
02:00:23,760 --> 02:00:26,039
All the tents will be repaired.

1302
02:00:26,240 --> 02:00:28,599
May Allah be pleased with you, Holofira Hatun.

1303
02:00:28,760 --> 02:00:31,559
You're taking care of us
despite all the troubles.

1304
02:00:31,640 --> 02:00:34,159
Don't mention it. This is my duty.

1305
02:00:34,720 --> 02:00:36,679
To make you feel comfortable.

1306
02:00:36,960 --> 02:00:40,359
Sister, I was looking for you everywhere.

1307
02:00:40,640 --> 02:00:42,159
You said you'd rest.

1308
02:00:42,320 --> 02:00:44,639
Fatma, I'm resting.

1309
02:00:44,960 --> 02:00:49,399
My resting is taking care of people's needs.

1310
02:00:49,840 --> 02:00:53,639
I'm not tiring myself, anyway.
Don't worry. I'm tiring the alps.

1311
02:00:54,960 --> 02:00:58,519
-Nokers are coming!
-They found our tribe!

1312
02:00:58,640 --> 02:01:01,159
Come on, you go!

1313
02:01:09,040 --> 02:01:11,999
My father and alps aren't
here. What should we do?

1314
02:01:12,000 --> 02:01:15,439
-We will fight. Hold the entrances, alps!
-Sisters, come on!

1315
02:01:16,040 --> 02:01:18,639
Hold the entrances! Fight!

1316
02:01:39,800 --> 02:01:43,519
-Draw back! Draw back!
-I will make Ulugan pay!

1317
02:01:43,640 --> 02:01:46,359
Wait! We have no time for this!

1318
02:02:06,800 --> 02:02:09,399
Is my precious living here?

1319
02:02:10,920 --> 02:02:12,919
Take me to her.

1320
02:02:12,960 --> 02:02:15,199
Almost there, Bala. Be patient.

1321
02:02:15,760 --> 02:02:18,239
Come on, Sofia. Come on.

1322
02:02:28,720 --> 02:02:32,199
Is she alright? Did anyone come?

1323
02:02:32,240 --> 02:02:35,279
No, she's been waiting for you for days.

1324
02:02:37,600 --> 02:02:39,719
It will be worth this.

1325
02:02:42,720 --> 02:02:44,919
I have a gift for her.

1326
02:02:51,400 --> 02:02:54,359
Move, move.

1327
02:03:20,800 --> 02:03:22,679
You demon.

1328
02:03:31,720 --> 02:03:34,279
Stop struggling in vain, Bala.

1329
02:03:36,400 --> 02:03:37,959
You lost.

1330
02:03:38,280 --> 02:03:40,679
Demon! You snake!

1331
02:03:40,920 --> 02:03:43,719
Where is my daughter?
What did you do to her, Sofia?

1332
02:03:44,840 --> 02:03:46,959
I didn't take you...

1333
02:03:48,840 --> 02:03:51,919
...to your daughter but your hell.

1334
02:03:54,360 --> 02:03:57,639
I was sure that you would fall into my trap.

1335
02:03:59,440 --> 02:04:01,839
I was going to take you down here...

1336
02:04:02,160 --> 02:04:06,559
...with a trick if something went wrong.

1337
02:04:07,400 --> 02:04:09,319
Right, Hristo?

1338
02:04:11,160 --> 02:04:13,479
We planned this before.

1339
02:04:17,000 --> 02:04:19,439
You're in my clutches again, Bala.

1340
02:04:29,400 --> 02:04:31,359
This is the end for you.

1341
02:04:31,880 --> 02:04:33,359
It was your trick, huh?

1342
02:04:33,480 --> 02:04:38,119
-I'll kill you. Where is my daughter?
-No, Bala. You played a trick too.

1343
02:04:39,400 --> 02:04:41,479
The difference is..

1344
02:04:42,400 --> 02:04:45,199
I ruined your game.

1345
02:04:46,480 --> 02:04:49,439
Your son and daughter-in-law...

1346
02:04:52,080 --> 02:04:53,559
...fell into my trap too.

1347
02:04:53,760 --> 02:04:57,799
If you hurt them, I will
give you such a death...

1348
02:04:58,920 --> 02:05:03,239
-I'll kill you, Sofia.
-You thought you'd meet Halime, huh?

1349
02:05:03,840 --> 02:05:07,079
You thought you'd meet Halime.

1350
02:05:08,120 --> 02:05:11,799
Today, you're going to lose Alaaddin too.

1351
02:05:13,800 --> 02:05:18,119
And you aren't going to die
before getting blind due to pain.

1352
02:05:22,160 --> 02:05:26,319
Alaaddin... No, my Alaaddin.

1353
02:05:29,480 --> 02:05:31,559
My Alaaddin.

1354
02:05:38,040 --> 02:05:40,799
-My Bey.
-Alps. My son.

1355
02:05:40,960 --> 02:05:43,439
Is everyone alright?

1356
02:05:46,040 --> 02:05:47,839
Is everyone alright?

1357
02:05:48,600 --> 02:05:53,439
-I'm fine, my Bey.
-We're good, my Bey.

1358
02:05:54,640 --> 02:05:58,079
My Bey... My Bey...

1359
02:06:00,760 --> 02:06:03,759
Where is Cerkutay Bey? Has anyone seen him?

1360
02:06:07,040 --> 02:06:11,839
-Cerkutay! My brother!
-Cerkutay!

1361
02:06:15,200 --> 02:06:18,199
My Bey, there he is! Cerkutay!

1362
02:06:18,560 --> 02:06:21,639
My brother! Cerkutay!

1363
02:06:23,120 --> 02:06:24,479
Get up.

1364
02:06:28,480 --> 02:06:30,319
Are you alright?

1365
02:06:30,600 --> 02:06:34,639
I'm fine, my Bey. I'm fine.

1366
02:06:48,920 --> 02:06:52,799
Pull yourself together. Are you alright?

1367
02:06:53,520 --> 02:06:56,159
I'm fine. I'm fine.

1368
02:06:56,440 --> 02:06:59,239
Come on, pull yourself together.

1369
02:06:59,920 --> 02:07:04,639
-Pull yourself together.
-I will be alright, my Bey.

1370
02:07:06,560 --> 02:07:10,239
-You're good, brother.
-Let's go to the tribe, Orhan.

1371
02:07:10,400 --> 02:07:13,999
-Alright, my Bey.
-My Bey, you go ahead.

1372
02:07:14,240 --> 02:07:16,079
We will come after you.

1373
02:07:16,320 --> 02:07:19,599
Cerkutay and the other alps aren't very well.

1374
02:07:19,720 --> 02:07:21,479
We'll come after you, my Bey.

1375
02:07:23,040 --> 02:07:24,919
Let's go, Orhan.

1376
02:07:28,960 --> 02:07:30,439
Brother.

1377
02:07:30,960 --> 02:07:34,679
I'm the messenger of the death.
You can't run away from me.

1378
02:07:34,960 --> 02:07:38,479
Osman and the alps aren't here.

1379
02:07:39,000 --> 02:07:43,799
Stop struggling in vain,
hatun. You will just die tired!

1380
02:07:44,800 --> 02:07:46,839
Attack, nokers!

1381
02:07:50,560 --> 02:07:52,319
Sisters, come on!

1382
02:09:59,520 --> 02:10:01,559
They did their part.

1383
02:10:02,000 --> 02:10:04,519
It's just the beginning, Sargun.

1384
02:10:05,560 --> 02:10:09,359
Osman is going to pay the price of his decision.

1385
02:10:09,560 --> 02:10:10,919
What's your plan?

1386
02:10:11,080 --> 02:10:14,239
I'm getting Osman's alps tracked.

1387
02:10:14,600 --> 02:10:20,519
I took them to the Kayi
tribe to let them follow.

1388
02:10:21,240 --> 02:10:25,559
Nokers are watching them from behind silently.

1389
02:10:26,520 --> 02:10:29,199
Osman's secret tribe.

1390
02:10:30,200 --> 02:10:32,559
I'll tell you where it is, Ulugan.

1391
02:10:33,320 --> 02:10:38,079
And when it's time, you will burn it down.

1392
02:10:39,760 --> 02:10:45,159
And Osman will go down
on his knees to beg like a dog!

1393
02:10:46,960 --> 02:10:51,759
Now it's only me who can
bring peace or war in these lands.

1394
02:10:53,240 --> 02:10:55,679
My sword is bloodthirsty, mother.

1395
02:10:56,240 --> 02:10:57,879
What are we waiting for?

1396
02:10:58,200 --> 02:10:59,319
Let's go.

1397
02:10:59,560 --> 02:11:01,279
Don't worry, son.

1398
02:11:02,280 --> 02:11:06,639
Your mother will give you blood if
you want blood and life if you want life.

1399
02:11:07,160 --> 02:11:08,279
Nokers!

1400
02:11:08,480 --> 02:11:10,759
Draw your swords and attack!

1401
02:11:39,640 --> 02:11:43,239
I never lose Bala. You will learn this.

1402
02:11:45,840 --> 02:11:49,159
I took your daughter from
you years ago, and today...

1403
02:11:49,880 --> 02:11:51,119
..I killed your son.

1404
02:11:51,120 --> 02:11:53,439
Even the devil would be ashamed of what you did!

1405
02:11:53,440 --> 02:11:56,279
Sofia, I will kill you in such a way that...

1406
02:11:56,280 --> 02:11:59,879
Stop with these threats, Bala.

1407
02:12:00,480 --> 02:12:01,519
Stop!

1408
02:12:05,360 --> 02:12:06,919
Cry for your son.

1409
02:12:10,320 --> 02:12:11,359
Sofia..

1410
02:12:11,720 --> 02:12:14,479
Because my soldiers killed him, Bala.

1411
02:12:14,800 --> 02:12:16,959
Sofia

1412
02:12:17,040 --> 02:12:20,519
Mother! Mother, where are you?
-Mother!

1413
02:12:20,680 --> 02:12:24,159
Alaeddin... Alaeddin

1414
02:12:28,120 --> 02:12:31,599
-Mother, where are you?
-Mother! -Mother!

1415
02:12:31,600 --> 02:12:34,159
-Mother!
-Mother, where are you? -Mother!

1416
02:12:34,160 --> 02:12:37,159
Where are you? Where are you mother?

1417
02:12:37,160 --> 02:12:40,919
Look everywhere! Mother!

1418
02:12:42,920 --> 02:12:44,799
Where are you?

1419
02:12:51,240 --> 02:12:53,319
Alaeddin, they are doing something.

1420
02:12:53,360 --> 02:12:57,599
Sofia's jackals have disguised
themselves as village's folk.

1421
02:12:57,800 --> 02:12:59,679
Damn it Hristo!

1422
02:13:00,720 --> 02:13:02,039
They survived!

1423
02:13:06,040 --> 02:13:07,599
Come with me!

1424
02:13:22,520 --> 02:13:24,479
Something is happening here.

1425
02:13:28,160 --> 02:13:29,359
Alaeddin!

1426
02:13:34,520 --> 02:13:35,785
My Gonca, are you alright?

1427
02:13:35,797 --> 02:13:37,319
I am, are you alright?
-I am.

1428
02:13:37,680 --> 02:13:38,679
Are you ready?

1429
02:13:38,800 --> 02:13:41,277
I am always ready.
Scholar. What about you?

1430
02:13:41,289 --> 02:13:42,119
Sure I am.

1431
02:13:42,200 --> 02:13:45,559
Now let's burn this village
down and save my mother.

1432
02:13:51,920 --> 02:13:53,119
Come, come here.

1433
02:13:54,200 --> 02:13:56,279
Kill all of them!

1434
02:14:17,400 --> 02:14:19,479
We ruined your trap Sofia.

1435
02:14:19,720 --> 02:14:21,999
Now there is no way out for you.

1436
02:14:23,600 --> 02:14:24,639
Come.

1437
02:14:24,920 --> 02:14:27,159
Come. Come and see.

1438
02:14:32,680 --> 02:14:35,919
You will never escape from here, Bala.

1439
02:14:38,320 --> 02:14:41,519
Come, come Sofia!

1440
02:15:02,720 --> 02:15:03,759
Father...

1441
02:15:08,440 --> 02:15:10,319
My Allah, protect them...

1442
02:15:17,680 --> 02:15:21,479
Ulugan, not even death will save you from me.

1443
02:15:22,320 --> 02:15:25,279
Come on!

1444
02:15:52,240 --> 02:15:56,799
My Allah, protect them... Protect them

1445
02:16:03,000 --> 02:16:04,399
Come here, you infidels!

1446
02:16:29,840 --> 02:16:33,159
What did you to my people? To my tribe?

1447
02:16:34,840 --> 02:16:38,199
My people... My tribe

1448
02:16:39,440 --> 02:16:41,558
We couldn't arrive on time, my Bey.

1449
02:16:54,120 --> 02:16:57,239
We could not.

1450
02:16:57,240 --> 02:16:59,199
They killed our poor people.

1451
02:17:00,080 --> 02:17:01,199
Ulugan!

1452
02:17:14,440 --> 02:17:16,199
They burned it down.

1453
02:17:24,240 --> 02:17:26,439
If my name is Osman Bey...

1454
02:17:26,799 --> 02:17:28,718
...I will bury you alive!

1455
02:17:29,480 --> 02:17:31,759
If my name is Osman Bey...

1456
02:17:32,520 --> 02:17:34,398
...I will put out these flames...

1457
02:17:34,400 --> 02:17:36,359
...with your blood.

1458
02:17:36,840 --> 02:17:38,959
Ulugan...

1459
02:17:43,520 --> 02:17:44,879
Fatma!

1460
02:17:44,879 --> 02:17:46,759
Holofira!

1461
02:18:22,440 --> 02:18:23,439
No...

1462
02:18:28,400 --> 02:18:29,439
Fatma!